			"parentCellId": "4cedaf68-408e-481a-8895-afcd92ae8b82"
		},
		"src/dbg/debugger.cpp-simstep-abbeb5e3-5b4b-466b-a5b7-354b3abfaf9d": {
			"path": "src/dbg/debugger.cpp-simstep-abbeb5e3-5b4b-466b-a5b7-354b3abfaf9d",
			"fileName": "debugger.cpp",
			"wiki": "The `cbSystemBreakpoint` callback is executed. It updates the GUI, logs the event, and based on user settings, pauses the debugger by acquiring a lock (`lock(WAITID_RUN)`). The debug loop is now blocked by `wait(WAITID_RUN)`, effectively pausing the debuggee until the user provides a command like 'run' or 'step'.",
			"cellName": "Flow: Init Debug - Handle System Breakpoint and Pause - debugger.cpp:L1793-1841",
			"cellId": "fc9d372f-58a8-437c-bd78-612c3d1470cd",
			"visible": true,
			"startLine": 1793,
			"endLine": 1841,
			"parentCellId": "4cedaf68-408e-481a-8895-afcd92ae8b82",
			"parentPath": "src/dbg/debugger.cpp",
			"simSteps": [
				{
					"simulationKey": "How debug execution control works",
					"simStepId": "abbeb5e3-5b4b-466b-a5b7-354b3abfaf9d"
				}
			]
		},
		"53732f1b-0247-441c-b695-22c8f19d13f7": {
			"path": "53732f1b-0247-441c-b695-22c8f19d13f7",
			"fileName": "53732f1b-0247-441c-b695-22c8f19d13f7",
			"cellName": "Flow: Run - User Issues 'run' Command - x64dbg.cpp:L148",
			"cellId": "53732f1b-0247-441c-b695-22c8f19d13f7",
			"visible": true,
			"parentCellId": "4baa9d03-cfb0-47b5-a48a-2e404daaa246"
		},
		"src/dbg/x64dbg.cpp-simstep-63aa1c5e-eb80-439a-a80d-4fd22ee0630b": {
			"path": "src/dbg/x64dbg.cpp-simstep-63aa1c5e-eb80-439a-a80d-4fd22ee0630b",
			"fileName": "x64dbg.cpp",
			"wiki": "When the debugger is paused, the user issues the 'run' command (or presses F9). This command is registered to the `cbDebugRun` callback.",
			"cellName": "Flow: Run - User Issues 'run' Command - x64dbg.cpp:L148",
			"cellId": "53732f1b-0247-441c-b695-22c8f19d13f7",
			"visible": true,
			"startLine": 148,
			"endLine": 148,
			"parentCellId": "4baa9d03-cfb0-47b5-a48a-2e404daaa246",
			"parentPath": "src/dbg/x64dbg.cpp",
			"simSteps": [
				{
					"simulationKey": "How debug execution control works",
					"simStepId": "63aa1c5e-eb80-439a-a80d-4fd22ee0630b"
				}
			]
		},
		"06e155f5-bf39-4d42-a95e-686d58d9d34f": {
			"path": "06e155f5-bf39-4d42-a95e-686d58d9d34f",
			"fileName": "06e155f5-bf39-4d42-a95e-686d58d9d34f",
			"cellName": "Flow: Run - Unlock the Debug Loop - cmd-debug-control.cpp:L56-62",
			"cellId": "06e155f5-bf39-4d42-a95e-686d58d9d34f",
			"visible": true,
			"parentCellId": "110ba731-9074-4a40-a86e-74cc73f27d55"
		},
		"src/dbg/commands/cmd-debug-control.cpp-simstep-32dbae95-4c6e-4f3e-b05d-b15ee68bbccf": {
			"path": "src/dbg/commands/cmd-debug-control.cpp-simstep-32dbae95-4c6e-4f3e-b05d-b15ee68bbccf",
			"fileName": "cmd-debug-control.cpp",
			"wiki": "The `cbDebugRunInternal` function checks if the debugger is already running using `dbgisrunning()`. Since it's paused, the check returns false. It then updates the GUI state to 'running' and, most importantly, calls `unlock(WAITID_RUN)`. This releases the lock that was holding the main debug loop.",
			"cellName": "Flow: Run - Unlock the Debug Loop - cmd-debug-control.cpp:L56-62",
			"cellId": "06e155f5-bf39-4d42-a95e-686d58d9d34f",
			"visible": true,
			"startLine": 56,
			"endLine": 62,
			"parentCellId": "110ba731-9074-4a40-a86e-74cc73f27d55",
			"parentPath": "src/dbg/commands/cmd-debug-control.cpp",
			"simSteps": [
				{
					"simulationKey": "How debug execution control works",
					"simStepId": "32dbae95-4c6e-4f3e-b05d-b15ee68bbccf"
				}
			]
		},
		"5ade3687-a5b4-4ffc-ab93-383749e6bd13": {
			"path": "5ade3687-a5b4-4ffc-ab93-383749e6bd13",
			"fileName": "5ade3687-a5b4-4ffc-ab93-383749e6bd13",
			"cellName": "Flow: Run - Debuggee is Running - debugger.h:L76",
			"cellId": "5ade3687-a5b4-4ffc-ab93-383749e6bd13",
			"visible": true,
			"parentCellId": "195ba16c-bc4b-4512-af6c-e28ebd08460f"
		},
		"src/dbg/debugger.h-simstep-bac07393-283d-45cd-ab19-3d9b8ee38781": {
			"path": "src/dbg/debugger.h-simstep-bac07393-283d-45cd-ab19-3d9b8ee38781",
			"fileName": "debugger.h",
			"wiki": "The `DebugLoop` continues to process OS debug events as they occur (exceptions, breakpoints, etc.). From the user's perspective, the program is now running until it hits a breakpoint or is paused again.",
			"cellName": "Flow: Run - Debuggee is Running - debugger.h:L76",
			"cellId": "5ade3687-a5b4-4ffc-ab93-383749e6bd13",
			"visible": true,
			"startLine": 76,
			"endLine": 76,
			"parentCellId": "195ba16c-bc4b-4512-af6c-e28ebd08460f",
			"parentPath": "src/dbg/debugger.h",
			"simSteps": [
				{
					"simulationKey": "How debug execution control works",
					"simStepId": "bac07393-283d-45cd-ab19-3d9b8ee38781"
				}
			]
		},
		"36c05c47-2b74-4fa9-80c1-8677015c4d34": {
			"path": "36c05c47-2b74-4fa9-80c1-8677015c4d34",
			"fileName": "36c05c47-2b74-4fa9-80c1-8677015c4d34",
			"cellName": "Flow: Pause - User Issues 'pause' Command - x64dbg.cpp:L151",
			"cellId": "36c05c47-2b74-4fa9-80c1-8677015c4d34",
			"visible": true,
			"parentCellId": "4baa9d03-cfb0-47b5-a48a-2e404daaa246"
		},
		"src/dbg/x64dbg.cpp-simstep-c727ab5d-6944-4924-99bb-507001b74ea0": {
			"path": "src/dbg/x64dbg.cpp-simstep-c727ab5d-6944-4924-99bb-507001b74ea0",
			"fileName": "x64dbg.cpp",
			"wiki": "While the debuggee is running, the user issues the 'pause' command. This is registered to the `cbDebugPause` callback.",
			"cellName": "Flow: Pause - User Issues 'pause' Command - x64dbg.cpp:L151",
			"cellId": "36c05c47-2b74-4fa9-80c1-8677015c4d34",
			"visible": true,
			"startLine": 151,
			"endLine": 151,
			"parentCellId": "4baa9d03-cfb0-47b5-a48a-2e404daaa246",
			"parentPath": "src/dbg/x64dbg.cpp",
			"simSteps": [
				{
					"simulationKey": "How debug execution control works",
					"simStepId": "c727ab5d-6944-4924-99bb-507001b74ea0"
				}
			]
		},
		"a81dd32a-c883-4f56-a91e-484584219931": {
			"path": "a81dd32a-c883-4f56-a91e-484584219931",
			"fileName": "a81dd32a-c883-4f56-a91e-484584219931",
			"cellName": "Flow: Pause - Set Temporary Breakpoint - cmd-debug-control.cpp:L394-429",
			"cellId": "a81dd32a-c883-4f56-a91e-484584219931",
			"visible": true,
			"parentCellId": "110ba731-9074-4a40-a86e-74cc73f27d55"
		},
		"src/dbg/commands/cmd-debug-control.cpp-simstep-ce8992b5-e886-4932-81e2-cc0e2e61a84f": {
			"path": "src/dbg/commands/cmd-debug-control.cpp-simstep-ce8992b5-e886-4932-81e2-cc0e2e61a84f",
			"fileName": "cmd-debug-control.cpp",
			"wiki": "The `cbDebugPause` function confirms the debuggee is running via `dbgisrunning()`. It then suspends the active thread, sets a temporary single-shot INT3 breakpoint at the current instruction pointer (CIP), and immediately resumes the thread. This forces the debuggee to break at its current location.",
			"cellName": "Flow: Pause - Set Temporary Breakpoint - cmd-debug-control.cpp:L394-429",
			"cellId": "a81dd32a-c883-4f56-a91e-484584219931",
			"visible": true,
			"startLine": 394,
			"endLine": 429,
			"parentCellId": "110ba731-9074-4a40-a86e-74cc73f27d55",
			"parentPath": "src/dbg/commands/cmd-debug-control.cpp",
			"simSteps": [
				{
					"simulationKey": "How debug execution control works",
					"simStepId": "ce8992b5-e886-4932-81e2-cc0e2e61a84f"
				}
			]
		},
		"4b9baf12-6ea0-44ba-9027-f03cc9e393b7": {
			"path": "4b9baf12-6ea0-44ba-9027-f03cc9e393b7",
			"fileName": "4b9baf12-6ea0-44ba-9027-f03cc9e393b7",
			"cellName": "Flow: Pause - Lock Debug Loop - debugger.cpp:L788-806",
			"cellId": "4b9baf12-6ea0-44ba-9027-f03cc9e393b7",
			"visible": true,
			"parentCellId": "4cedaf68-408e-481a-8895-afcd92ae8b82"
		},
		"src/dbg/debugger.cpp-simstep-ba589bea-0433-4b28-9ca1-044ebccf15bd": {
			"path": "src/dbg/debugger.cpp-simstep-ba589bea-0433-4b28-9ca1-044ebccf15bd",
			"fileName": "debugger.cpp",
			"wiki": "The `cbPauseBreakpoint` function is executed. It removes the temporary breakpoint it just hit, updates the GUI to the 'paused' state, and crucially calls `lock(WAITID_RUN)`. This blocks the `DebugLoop` from continuing, pausing execution.",
			"cellName": "Flow: Pause - Lock Debug Loop - debugger.cpp:L788-806",
			"cellId": "4b9baf12-6ea0-44ba-9027-f03cc9e393b7",
			"visible": true,
			"startLine": 788,
			"endLine": 806,
			"parentCellId": "4cedaf68-408e-481a-8895-afcd92ae8b82",
			"parentPath": "src/dbg/debugger.cpp",
			"simSteps": [
				{
					"simulationKey": "How debug execution control works",
					"simStepId": "ba589bea-0433-4b28-9ca1-044ebccf15bd"
				}
			]
		},
		"a1cb526f-042b-459c-9882-d8457d9686b9": {
			"path": "a1cb526f-042b-459c-9882-d8457d9686b9",
			"fileName": "a1cb526f-042b-459c-9882-d8457d9686b9",
			"cellName": "Flow: Step - User Issues 'step' Command - x64dbg.cpp:L153-156",
			"cellId": "a1cb526f-042b-459c-9882-d8457d9686b9",
			"visible": true,
			"parentCellId": "4baa9d03-cfb0-47b5-a48a-2e404daaa246"
		},
		"src/dbg/x64dbg.cpp-simstep-a56744f7-c673-4615-8806-fc4814fd3c1e": {
			"path": "src/dbg/x64dbg.cpp-simstep-a56744f7-c673-4615-8806-fc4814fd3c1e",
			"fileName": "x64dbg.cpp",
			"wiki": "When paused, the user issues a stepping command, such as 'stepinto' (F7) or 'stepover' (F8). These commands are registered to `cbDebugStepInto` and `cbDebugStepOver` respectively.",
			"cellName": "Flow: Step - User Issues 'step' Command - x64dbg.cpp:L153-156",
			"cellId": "a1cb526f-042b-459c-9882-d8457d9686b9",
			"visible": true,
			"startLine": 153,
			"endLine": 156,
			"parentCellId": "4baa9d03-cfb0-47b5-a48a-2e404daaa246",
			"parentPath": "src/dbg/x64dbg.cpp",
			"simSteps": [
				{
					"simulationKey": "How debug execution control works",
					"simStepId": "a56744f7-c673-4615-8806-fc4814fd3c1e"
				}
			]
		},
		"e8a08968-e1d9-464c-b23c-c60818c9f680": {
			"path": "e8a08968-e1d9-464c-b23c-c60818c9f680",
			"fileName": "e8a08968-e1d9-464c-b23c-c60818c9f680",
			"cellName": "Flow: Step - Configure Step and Unlock Debug Loop - cmd-debug-control.cpp:L457-459",
			"cellId": "e8a08968-e1d9-464c-b23c-c60818c9f680",
			"visible": true,
			"parentCellId": "110ba731-9074-4a40-a86e-74cc73f27d55"
		},
		"src/dbg/commands/cmd-debug-control.cpp-simstep-2b1756b2-6bc7-4e7e-bb99-9c8d07fa70e2": {
			"path": "src/dbg/commands/cmd-debug-control.cpp-simstep-2b1756b2-6bc7-4e7e-bb99-9c8d07fa70e2",
			"fileName": "cmd-debug-control.cpp",
			"wiki": "The step handler (`cbDebugStepInto` or `cbDebugStepOver`) configures the debug engine for the desired step type by calling `StepIntoWow64` or `StepOverWrapper`, providing `cbStep` as the callback. It then calls `cbDebugRunInternal` to `unlock(WAITID_RUN)`, allowing the debug loop to proceed for a single step.",
			"cellName": "Flow: Step - Configure Step and Unlock Debug Loop - cmd-debug-control.cpp:L457-459",
			"cellId": "e8a08968-e1d9-464c-b23c-c60818c9f680",
			"visible": true,
			"startLine": 457,
			"endLine": 459,
			"parentCellId": "110ba731-9074-4a40-a86e-74cc73f27d55",
			"parentPath": "src/dbg/commands/cmd-debug-control.cpp",
			"simSteps": [
				{
					"simulationKey": "How debug execution control works",
					"simStepId": "2b1756b2-6bc7-4e7e-bb99-9c8d07fa70e2"
				}
			]
		},
		"7fb45274-be79-45b5-a578-f7ad58f69682": {
			"path": "7fb45274-be79-45b5-a578-f7ad58f69682",
			"fileName": "7fb45274-be79-45b5-a578-f7ad58f69682",
			"cellName": "Flow: Step - Handle Step Completion and Pause - debugger.cpp:L1302-1329",
			"cellId": "7fb45274-be79-45b5-a578-f7ad58f69682",
			"visible": true,
			"parentCellId": "4cedaf68-408e-481a-8895-afcd92ae8b82"
		},
		"src/dbg/debugger.cpp-simstep-222eaab1-3388-4c1c-8ca6-43170482a57d": {
			"path": "src/dbg/debugger.cpp-simstep-222eaab1-3388-4c1c-8ca6-43170482a57d",
			"fileName": "debugger.cpp",
			"wiki": "The `cbStep` callback is executed. It updates the GUI to the 'paused' state, re-locks the debug loop by calling `lock(WAITID_RUN)`, and then waits for the next user command. The debugger is now paused at the next instruction.",
			"cellName": "Flow: Step - Handle Step Completion and Pause - debugger.cpp:L1302-1329",
			"cellId": "7fb45274-be79-45b5-a578-f7ad58f69682",
			"visible": true,
			"startLine": 1302,
			"endLine": 1329,
			"parentCellId": "4cedaf68-408e-481a-8895-afcd92ae8b82",
			"parentPath": "src/dbg/debugger.cpp",
			"simSteps": [
				{
					"simulationKey": "How debug execution control works",
					"simStepId": "222eaab1-3388-4c1c-8ca6-43170482a57d"
				}
			]
		},
