		"src/dbg/breakpoint.cpp-simstep-01a1efc9-d0d8-439b-b047-69b093313a0f": {
			"path": "src/dbg/breakpoint.cpp-simstep-01a1efc9-d0d8-439b-b047-69b093313a0f",
			"fileName": "breakpoint.cpp",
			"wiki": "The `BpNew` function allocates a new `BREAKPOINT` struct, populates it with details like address, type, and original bytes, and then adds it to the global 'breakpoints' map, making it known to the debugger.",
			"cellName": "Software Breakpoint: BpNew Adds to Internal List - breakpoint.cpp:L102-158",
			"cellId": "52a5928c-1b8d-4748-8324-022a0618d0db",
