		"src/gui/Src/Gui/MemoryMapView.cpp-simstep-295fa825-f09a-45d5-98a7-0e403d7ff52f": {
			"path": "src/gui/Src/Gui/MemoryMapView.cpp-simstep-295fa825-f09a-45d5-98a7-0e403d7ff52f",
			"fileName": "MemoryMapView.cpp",
			"wiki": "The `refreshMapSlot` function iterates through the received memory map data, populating the table view with details for each memory region, such as address, size, protection, and type. It then calls `reloadData` to repaint the view.",
			"cellName": "GUI: Populate Memory Map View - MemoryMapView.cpp:L475-578",
			"cellId": "2ae4fb04-1731-48e3-b64b-5b45bfd1aa43",
			"visible": true,
			"startLine": 475,
			"endLine": 578,
			"parentCellId": "38a573c4-e2b4-43be-b790-84c3d33d5b64",
			"parentPath": "src/gui/Src/Gui/MemoryMapView.cpp",
			"simSteps": [
				{
					"simulationKey": "How memory viewing and patching works",
					"simStepId": "295fa825-f09a-45d5-98a7-0e403d7ff52f"
				}
			]
		},
		"65ba6020-8419-4fae-8329-6954dcb74763": {
			"path": "65ba6020-8419-4fae-8329-6954dcb74763",
			"fileName": "65ba6020-8419-4fae-8329-6954dcb74763",
			"cellName": "GUI: Open Assemble Dialog - CPUDisassembly.cpp:L892-973",
			"cellId": "65ba6020-8419-4fae-8329-6954dcb74763",
			"visible": true,
			"parentCellId": "0b54dc6a-c70d-4ce9-b443-c72eddfea91b"
		},
		"src/gui/Src/Gui/CPUDisassembly.cpp-simstep-85531d93-a019-42d0-a6ab-88062eaffffd": {
			"path": "src/gui/Src/Gui/CPUDisassembly.cpp-simstep-85531d93-a019-42d0-a6ab-88062eaffffd",
			"fileName": "CPUDisassembly.cpp",
			"wiki": "The `assembleSlot` in `CPUDisassembly.cpp` is executed. It opens the `AssembleDialog`, allowing the user to input a new assembly instruction. Upon confirmation, it calls `DbgFunctions()->AssembleAtEx` to process the new instruction.",
			"cellName": "GUI: Open Assemble Dialog - CPUDisassembly.cpp:L892-973",
			"cellId": "65ba6020-8419-4fae-8329-6954dcb74763",
			"visible": true,
			"startLine": 892,
			"endLine": 973,
			"parentCellId": "0b54dc6a-c70d-4ce9-b443-c72eddfea91b",
			"parentPath": "src/gui/Src/Gui/CPUDisassembly.cpp",
			"simSteps": [
				{
					"simulationKey": "How memory viewing and patching works",
					"simStepId": "85531d93-a019-42d0-a6ab-88062eaffffd"
				}
			]
		},
		"f1a10fa7-b91f-4cf6-a760-ba617fd51b9a": {
			"path": "f1a10fa7-b91f-4cf6-a760-ba617fd51b9a",
			"fileName": "f1a10fa7-b91f-4cf6-a760-ba617fd51b9a",
			"cellName": "Debugger Core: Patch Memory - memory.cpp:L746-774",
			"cellId": "f1a10fa7-b91f-4cf6-a760-ba617fd51b9a",
			"visible": true,
			"parentCellId": "4db798ca-f5a3-489c-8705-a9eb24ceda97"
		},
		"src/dbg/memory.cpp-simstep-8c27b85b-10db-43c2-b3b1-23300b83a06f": {
			"path": "src/dbg/memory.cpp-simstep-8c27b85b-10db-43c2-b3b1-23300b83a06f",
			"fileName": "memory.cpp",
			"wiki": "The `MemPatch` function in `memory.cpp` first reads the original bytes from the target address (`MemRead`), then writes the new bytes (`MemWrite`), and finally calls `PatchSet` to record the modification.",
			"cellName": "Debugger Core: Patch Memory - memory.cpp:L746-774",
			"cellId": "f1a10fa7-b91f-4cf6-a760-ba617fd51b9a",
			"visible": true,
			"startLine": 746,
			"endLine": 774,
			"parentCellId": "4db798ca-f5a3-489c-8705-a9eb24ceda97",
			"parentPath": "src/dbg/memory.cpp",
			"simSteps": [
				{
					"simulationKey": "How memory viewing and patching works",
					"simStepId": "8c27b85b-10db-43c2-b3b1-23300b83a06f"
				}
			]
		},
		"f010d7a4-2b77-473c-8337-301b497a4eb0": {
			"path": "f010d7a4-2b77-473c-8337-301b497a4eb0",
			"fileName": "f010d7a4-2b77-473c-8337-301b497a4eb0",
			"cellName": "Debugger Core: Track Patch - patches.cpp:L16-20",
			"cellId": "f010d7a4-2b77-473c-8337-301b497a4eb0",
			"visible": true,
			"parentCellId": "e1cc2458-579d-49b0-8c06-511c7059d927"
		},
		"src/dbg/patches.cpp-simstep-6b41a7f9-c245-4e49-a1fd-df2c668a45f4": {
			"path": "src/dbg/patches.cpp-simstep-6b41a7f9-c245-4e49-a1fd-df2c668a45f4",
			"fileName": "patches.cpp",
			"wiki": "The `PatchSet` function in `patches.cpp` adds or updates a `PATCHINFO` structure in a global map. This map keeps track of all memory modifications, storing the address, original byte, and new byte.",
			"cellName": "Debugger Core: Track Patch - patches.cpp:L16-20",
			"cellId": "f010d7a4-2b77-473c-8337-301b497a4eb0",
			"visible": true,
			"startLine": 16,
			"endLine": 20,
			"parentCellId": "e1cc2458-579d-49b0-8c06-511c7059d927",
			"parentPath": "src/dbg/patches.cpp",
			"simSteps": [
				{
					"simulationKey": "How memory viewing and patching works",
					"simStepId": "6b41a7f9-c245-4e49-a1fd-df2c668a45f4"
				}
			]
		},
		"8ca60ead-5682-4729-a6f3-696ded7471e7": {
			"path": "8ca60ead-5682-4729-a6f3-696ded7471e7",
			"fileName": "8ca60ead-5682-4729-a6f3-696ded7471e7",
			"cellName": "GUI: Receive Patch Update Signal and Refresh Patches Dialog - PatchDialog.cpp:L181-618",
			"cellId": "8ca60ead-5682-4729-a6f3-696ded7471e7",
			"visible": true,
			"parentCellId": "78c32eae-2bc4-4a08-ba02-c53c958b896e"
		},
		"src/gui/Src/Gui/PatchDialog.cpp-simstep-f983191d-7edd-4b1b-9887-bca0772ef83d": {
			"path": "src/gui/Src/Gui/PatchDialog.cpp-simstep-f983191d-7edd-4b1b-9887-bca0772ef83d",
			"fileName": "PatchDialog.cpp",
			"wiki": "The `PatchDialog` receives the `updatePatches` signal. It calls `DbgFunctions()->PatchEnum` to get the latest list of all patches from the debugger core and repopulates its list view.",
			"cellName": "GUI: Receive Patch Update Signal and Refresh Patches Dialog - PatchDialog.cpp:L181-618",
			"cellId": "8ca60ead-5682-4729-a6f3-696ded7471e7",
			"visible": true,
			"startLine": 181,
			"endLine": 618,
			"parentCellId": "78c32eae-2bc4-4a08-ba02-c53c958b896e",
			"parentPath": "src/gui/Src/Gui/PatchDialog.cpp",
			"simSteps": [
				{
					"simulationKey": "How memory viewing and patching works",
					"simStepId": "f983191d-7edd-4b1b-9887-bca0772ef83d"
				}
			]
		},
		"769da604-425b-48bd-8779-8e96f7e869a8": {
			"path": "769da604-425b-48bd-8779-8e96f7e869a8",
			"fileName": "769da604-425b-48bd-8779-8e96f7e869a8",
			"cellName": "GUI: Restore Original Byte - PatchDialog.cpp:L290-292",
			"cellId": "769da604-425b-48bd-8779-8e96f7e869a8",
			"visible": true,
			"parentCellId": "78c32eae-2bc4-4a08-ba02-c53c958b896e"
		},
		"src/gui/Src/Gui/PatchDialog.cpp-simstep-32b478f9-c688-47eb-b58a-4c27f5e2303d": {
			"path": "src/gui/Src/Gui/PatchDialog.cpp-simstep-32b478f9-c688-47eb-b58a-4c27f5e2303d",
			"fileName": "PatchDialog.cpp",
			"wiki": "The `on_listPatches_itemChanged` slot determines that the patch was unchecked and calls `DbgMemWrite` to write the original byte back to the target memory address, effectively disabling the patch.",
			"cellName": "GUI: Restore Original Byte - PatchDialog.cpp:L290-292",
			"cellId": "769da604-425b-48bd-8779-8e96f7e869a8",
			"visible": true,
			"startLine": 290,
			"endLine": 292,
			"parentCellId": "78c32eae-2bc4-4a08-ba02-c53c958b896e",
			"parentPath": "src/gui/Src/Gui/PatchDialog.cpp",
			"simSteps": [
				{
					"simulationKey": "How memory viewing and patching works",
					"simStepId": "32b478f9-c688-47eb-b58a-4c27f5e2303d"
				}
			]
		},
		"8f81fd69-f4a0-4abb-b12b-e75b1bd0da92": {
			"path": "8f81fd69-f4a0-4abb-b12b-e75b1bd0da92",
			"fileName": "8f81fd69-f4a0-4abb-b12b-e75b1bd0da92",
			"cellName": "GUI: Execute 'savedata' Command - MemoryMapView.cpp:L725-756",
			"cellId": "8f81fd69-f4a0-4abb-b12b-e75b1bd0da92",
