		"abd9e4b3-ddfe-490f-9f1d-7660d5ceeed7": {
			"path": "abd9e4b3-ddfe-490f-9f1d-7660d5ceeed7",
			"fileName": "abd9e4b3-ddfe-490f-9f1d-7660d5ceeed7",
			"cellName": "Command Flow: User Input - x64dbg.cpp:L511-526",
			"cellId": "abd9e4b3-ddfe-490f-9f1d-7660d5ceeed7",
			"visible": true,
			"parentCellId": "4baa9d03-cfb0-47b5-a48a-2e404daaa246"
		},
		"src/dbg/x64dbg.cpp-simstep-96833474-7463-42fd-baee-075aab0dafe4": {
			"path": "src/dbg/x64dbg.cpp-simstep-96833474-7463-42fd-baee-075aab0dafe4",
			"fileName": "x64dbg.cpp",
			"wiki": "The user types a command like `inc rax` or `scriptexec \"C:\\myscript.txt\"` into the GUI's command bar. The GUI sends this command string to a message queue for the debugger's command processing thread.",
			"cellName": "Command Flow: User Input - x64dbg.cpp:L511-526",
			"cellId": "abd9e4b3-ddfe-490f-9f1d-7660d5ceeed7",
			"visible": true,
			"startLine": 511,
			"endLine": 526,
			"parentCellId": "4baa9d03-cfb0-47b5-a48a-2e404daaa246",
			"parentPath": "src/dbg/x64dbg.cpp",
			"simSteps": [
				{
					"simulationKey": "How the command line and scripting works",
					"simStepId": "96833474-7463-42fd-baee-075aab0dafe4"
				}
			]
		},
		"076c7e7b-c67b-48cd-892d-e2d33910b184": {
			"path": "076c7e7b-c67b-48cd-892d-e2d33910b184",
			"fileName": "076c7e7b-c67b-48cd-892d-e2d33910b184",
			"cellName": "Command Flow: Command Splitting - command.cpp:L281-290",
			"cellId": "076c7e7b-c67b-48cd-892d-e2d33910b184",
			"visible": true,
			"parentCellId": "08ad24f4-4d15-4978-8386-5edb774661ab"
		},
		"src/dbg/command.cpp-simstep-3f3015b4-c26c-49de-b83d-ac4cf4b1f3af": {
			"path": "src/dbg/command.cpp-simstep-3f3015b4-c26c-49de-b83d-ac4cf4b1f3af",
			"fileName": "command.cpp",
			"wiki": "The `cmdloop` function receives the command string and calls `cmdsplit` to break it into individual commands based on the semicolon (`;`) separator. This allows for chaining multiple commands.",
			"cellName": "Command Flow: Command Splitting - command.cpp:L281-290",
			"cellId": "076c7e7b-c67b-48cd-892d-e2d33910b184",
			"visible": true,
			"startLine": 281,
			"endLine": 290,
			"parentCellId": "08ad24f4-4d15-4978-8386-5edb774661ab",
			"parentPath": "src/dbg/command.cpp",
			"simSteps": [
				{
					"simulationKey": "How the command line and scripting works",
					"simStepId": "3f3015b4-c26c-49de-b83d-ac4cf4b1f3af"
				}
			]
		},
		"11577fa5-40c5-4693-a9d7-f531ef7570d0": {
			"path": "11577fa5-40c5-4693-a9d7-f531ef7570d0",
			"fileName": "11577fa5-40c5-4693-a9d7-f531ef7570d0",
			"cellName": "Command Flow: Command Lookup and Callback - command.cpp:L297-315",
			"cellId": "11577fa5-40c5-4693-a9d7-f531ef7570d0",
			"visible": true,
			"parentCellId": "08ad24f4-4d15-4978-8386-5edb774661ab"
		},
		"src/dbg/command.cpp-simstep-43850d6a-42fe-4c32-9997-24678bbe14b2": {
			"path": "src/dbg/command.cpp-simstep-43850d6a-42fe-4c32-9997-24678bbe14b2",
			"fileName": "command.cpp",
			"wiki": "Inside the `cmdloop`, `cmdget` finds the registered `COMMAND` structure for the command name (e.g., 'inc'). `cmdexeccallback` is then invoked, which parses arguments and calls the command's specific C++ callback function, in this case `cbInstrInc`.",
			"cellName": "Command Flow: Command Lookup and Callback - command.cpp:L297-315",
			"cellId": "11577fa5-40c5-4693-a9d7-f531ef7570d0",
			"visible": true,
			"startLine": 297,
			"endLine": 315,
			"parentCellId": "08ad24f4-4d15-4978-8386-5edb774661ab",
			"parentPath": "src/dbg/command.cpp",
			"simSteps": [
				{
					"simulationKey": "How the command line and scripting works",
					"simStepId": "43850d6a-42fe-4c32-9997-24678bbe14b2"
				}
			]
		},
		"cf6ccd20-517c-4557-984e-4431003622fe": {
			"path": "cf6ccd20-517c-4557-984e-4431003622fe",
			"fileName": "cf6ccd20-517c-4557-984e-4431003622fe",
			"cellName": "Command Flow: Direct Execution / Expression Fallback - command.cpp:L326-345",
			"cellId": "cf6ccd20-517c-4557-984e-4431003622fe",
			"visible": true,
			"parentCellId": "08ad24f4-4d15-4978-8386-5edb774661ab"
		},
		"src/dbg/command.cpp-simstep-0c1d9a7c-58e1-4e6b-b18f-858cb52d5a67": {
			"path": "src/dbg/command.cpp-simstep-0c1d9a7c-58e1-4e6b-b18f-858cb52d5a67",
			"fileName": "command.cpp",
			"wiki": "`cmddirectexec` is called to execute the transformed command `rax++`. It first tries to find a registered command with this name. When it fails, it falls back to treating the string as an expression to be evaluated by the `ExpressionParser`.",
			"cellName": "Command Flow: Direct Execution / Expression Fallback - command.cpp:L326-345",
			"cellId": "cf6ccd20-517c-4557-984e-4431003622fe",
			"visible": true,
			"startLine": 326,
			"endLine": 345,
			"parentCellId": "08ad24f4-4d15-4978-8386-5edb774661ab",
			"parentPath": "src/dbg/command.cpp",
			"simSteps": [
				{
					"simulationKey": "How the command line and scripting works",
					"simStepId": "0c1d9a7c-58e1-4e6b-b18f-858cb52d5a67"
				}
			]
		},
		"43801730-e66e-489a-bd22-6ea1d763a137": {
			"path": "43801730-e66e-489a-bd22-6ea1d763a137",
			"fileName": "43801730-e66e-489a-bd22-6ea1d763a137",
			"cellName": "Command Flow: Expression Evaluation - expressionparser.cpp:L300-301",
			"cellId": "43801730-e66e-489a-bd22-6ea1d763a137",
			"visible": true,
			"parentCellId": "857b5934-a054-45ff-93e1-dfa6e66cdf45"
		},
		"src/dbg/expressionparser.cpp-simstep-a02b0feb-2c4c-4841-97cd-50985bc8711c": {
			"path": "src/dbg/expressionparser.cpp-simstep-a02b0feb-2c4c-4841-97cd-50985bc8711c",
			"fileName": "expressionparser.cpp",
			"wiki": "The `ExpressionParser::Calculate` method parses the expression. It identifies `rax` as a register, reads its current value, performs the post-increment operation, and writes the new value back to the `rax` register, completing the command.",
			"cellName": "Command Flow: Expression Evaluation - expressionparser.cpp:L300-301",
			"cellId": "43801730-e66e-489a-bd22-6ea1d763a137",
			"visible": true,
			"startLine": 300,
			"endLine": 301,
			"parentCellId": "857b5934-a054-45ff-93e1-dfa6e66cdf45",
			"parentPath": "src/dbg/expressionparser.cpp",
			"simSteps": [
				{
					"simulationKey": "How the command line and scripting works",
					"simStepId": "a02b0feb-2c4c-4841-97cd-50985bc8711c"
				}
			]
		},
		"910570e9-40e2-4ae3-9967-6f2150b76205": {
			"path": "910570e9-40e2-4ae3-9967-6f2150b76205",
			"fileName": "910570e9-40e2-4ae3-9967-6f2150b76205",
			"cellName": "Scripting Flow: User issues 'scriptexec' command - cmd-script.cpp:L55-60",
			"cellId": "910570e9-40e2-4ae3-9967-6f2150b76205",
			"visible": true,
			"parentCellId": "e9f3190b-0159-4b2a-a009-b6ae46af593f"
		},
		"src/dbg/commands/cmd-script.cpp-simstep-31f0fba5-8901-4231-9ec4-da4cc520d606": {
			"path": "src/dbg/commands/cmd-script.cpp-simstep-31f0fba5-8901-4231-9ec4-da4cc520d606",
			"fileName": "cmd-script.cpp",
			"wiki": "The user enters the `scriptexec` command. After being processed by `cmdloop`, the command's registered callback `cbScriptExec` is called.",
			"cellName": "Scripting Flow: User issues 'scriptexec' command - cmd-script.cpp:L55-60",
			"cellId": "910570e9-40e2-4ae3-9967-6f2150b76205",
			"visible": true,
			"startLine": 55,
			"endLine": 60,
			"parentCellId": "e9f3190b-0159-4b2a-a009-b6ae46af593f",
			"parentPath": "src/dbg/commands/cmd-script.cpp",
			"simSteps": [
				{
					"simulationKey": "How the command line and scripting works",
					"simStepId": "31f0fba5-8901-4231-9ec4-da4cc520d606"
				}
			]
		},
		"2c8b849a-ee2f-4860-86bf-2b11901c3c7d": {
			"path": "2c8b849a-ee2f-4860-86bf-2b11901c3c7d",
			"fileName": "2c8b849a-ee2f-4860-86bf-2b11901c3c7d",
			"cellName": "Scripting Flow: Load and Run Script - simplescript.cpp:L833-843",
			"cellId": "2c8b849a-ee2f-4860-86bf-2b11901c3c7d",
			"visible": true,
			"parentCellId": "0c0c5dd5-1912-4c4e-a7f7-61cfa0c8634b"
		},
		"src/dbg/simplescript.cpp-simstep-82be4420-8561-4b5a-a265-0fcf9b7b960a": {
			"path": "src/dbg/simplescript.cpp-simstep-82be4420-8561-4b5a-a265-0fcf9b7b960a",
			"fileName": "simplescript.cpp",
			"wiki": "`ScriptExecAwait` queues a task that first calls `scriptLoad` to read and parse the script file into an internal line map. It then calls `scriptRun` to begin executing the script from the first line.",
			"cellName": "Scripting Flow: Load and Run Script - simplescript.cpp:L833-843",
			"cellId": "2c8b849a-ee2f-4860-86bf-2b11901c3c7d",
			"visible": true,
			"startLine": 833,
			"endLine": 843,
			"parentCellId": "0c0c5dd5-1912-4c4e-a7f7-61cfa0c8634b",
			"parentPath": "src/dbg/simplescript.cpp",
			"simSteps": [
				{
					"simulationKey": "How the command line and scripting works",
					"simStepId": "82be4420-8561-4b5a-a265-0fcf9b7b960a"
				}
			]
		},
		"94454940-4060-4f7e-a84c-aea4d3d21bb9": {
			"path": "94454940-4060-4f7e-a84c-aea4d3d21bb9",
			"fileName": "94454940-4060-4f7e-a84c-aea4d3d21bb9",
			"cellName": "Scripting Flow: Merged Command Execution - command.cpp:L326-345",
			"cellId": "94454940-4060-4f7e-a84c-aea4d3d21bb9",
			"visible": true,
			"parentCellId": "08ad24f4-4d15-4978-8386-5edb774661ab"
		},
		"src/dbg/command.cpp-simstep-d6cefb4e-8466-45bd-8314-2c450f758227": {
			"path": "src/dbg/command.cpp-simstep-d6cefb4e-8466-45bd-8314-2c450f758227",
			"fileName": "command.cpp",
			"wiki": "The script engine has invoked `cmddirectexec`. The execution flow now merges with the standard command flow. `cmddirectexec` will resolve `inc rax` to its callback (`cbInstrInc`), which transforms it to `rax++`, which is finally executed by the `ExpressionParser`.",
			"cellName": "Scripting Flow: Merged Command Execution - command.cpp:L326-345",
			"cellId": "94454940-4060-4f7e-a84c-aea4d3d21bb9",
			"visible": true,
			"startLine": 326,
			"endLine": 345,
			"parentCellId": "08ad24f4-4d15-4978-8386-5edb774661ab",
			"parentPath": "src/dbg/command.cpp",
			"simSteps": [
				{
					"simulationKey": "How the command line and scripting works",
					"simStepId": "d6cefb4e-8466-45bd-8314-2c450f758227"
				}
			]
		},
		"0c1996ea-84d1-4973-b85e-fe1aaea2781b": {
			"path": "0c1996ea-84d1-4973-b85e-fe1aaea2781b",
			"fileName": "0c1996ea-84d1-4973-b85e-fe1aaea2781b",
			"cellName": "Scripting Flow: Script Loop Continues - simplescript.cpp:L608-612",
			"cellId": "0c1996ea-84d1-4973-b85e-fe1aaea2781b",
			"visible": true,
			"parentCellId": "0c0c5dd5-1912-4c4e-a7f7-61cfa0c8634b"
		},
		"src/dbg/simplescript.cpp-simstep-1081c258-b893-4c3a-b57d-5fcac8faed30": {
			"path": "src/dbg/simplescript.cpp-simstep-1081c258-b893-4c3a-b57d-5fcac8faed30",
			"fileName": "simplescript.cpp",
			"wiki": "The `scriptInternalCmdExec` function returns a `STATUS_CONTINUE` code, signaling to the `scriptRun` loop that execution was successful and it should proceed to the next line of the script.",
			"cellName": "Scripting Flow: Script Loop Continues - simplescript.cpp:L608-612",
			"cellId": "0c1996ea-84d1-4973-b85e-fe1aaea2781b",
			"visible": true,
			"startLine": 608,
			"endLine": 612,
			"parentCellId": "0c0c5dd5-1912-4c4e-a7f7-61cfa0c8634b",
			"parentPath": "src/dbg/simplescript.cpp",
			"simSteps": [
				{
					"simulationKey": "How the command line and scripting works",
					"simStepId": "1081c258-b893-4c3a-b57d-5fcac8faed30"
				}
			]
		},
		"db48773a-d8ad-42ea-9350-c9c2700e7fb7": {
			"path": "db48773a-d8ad-42ea-9350-c9c2700e7fb7",
			"fileName": "db48773a-d8ad-42ea-9350-c9c2700e7fb7",
			"cellName": "Scripting Flow: Script Unload - simplescript.cpp:L841",
