		"1d6872cc-f613-4495-9676-6175e9191fb0": {
			"path": "1d6872cc-f613-4495-9676-6175e9191fb0",
			"fileName": "1d6872cc-f613-4495-9676-6175e9191fb0",
			"cellName": "User Starts Trace Recording - x64dbg.cpp:L271",
			"cellId": "1d6872cc-f613-4495-9676-6175e9191fb0",
			"visible": true,
			"parentCellId": "4baa9d03-cfb0-47b5-a48a-2e404daaa246"
		},
		"src/dbg/x64dbg.cpp-simstep-1b490872-5117-45bb-8bc8-dfd6470cb299": {
			"path": "src/dbg/x64dbg.cpp-simstep-1b490872-5117-45bb-8bc8-dfd6470cb299",
			"fileName": "x64dbg.cpp",
			"wiki": "A user initiates execution tracing by issuing the `StartRunTrace` command, often through the GUI's context menu or by typing it directly. This command is an alias for `StartTraceRecording` and is registered at startup to map to the `cbDebugStartTraceRecording` callback function.",
			"cellName": "User Starts Trace Recording - x64dbg.cpp:L271",
			"cellId": "1d6872cc-f613-4495-9676-6175e9191fb0",
			"visible": true,
			"startLine": 271,
			"endLine": 271,
			"parentCellId": "4baa9d03-cfb0-47b5-a48a-2e404daaa246",
			"parentPath": "src/dbg/x64dbg.cpp",
			"simSteps": [
				{
					"simulationKey": "How execution tracing works",
					"simStepId": "1b490872-5117-45bb-8bc8-dfd6470cb299"
				}
			]
		},
		"2782195b-68d7-41dc-9fa4-247e256cab9d": {
			"path": "2782195b-68d7-41dc-9fa4-247e256cab9d",
			"fileName": "2782195b-68d7-41dc-9fa4-247e256cab9d",
			"cellName": "Handle Start Trace Command - cmd-tracing.cpp:L234-239",
			"cellId": "2782195b-68d7-41dc-9fa4-247e256cab9d",
			"visible": true,
			"parentCellId": "b23dc46d-f8ba-437a-9906-3b8abc585040"
		},
		"src/dbg/commands/cmd-tracing.cpp-simstep-f73b0031-4cdf-428f-82a9-345d3e43ebb4": {
			"path": "src/dbg/commands/cmd-tracing.cpp-simstep-f73b0031-4cdf-428f-82a9-345d3e43ebb4",
			"fileName": "cmd-tracing.cpp",
			"wiki": "The `cbDebugStartTraceRecording` function is executed. It validates that a filename argument is provided and then calls the `enableTraceRecording` method on the global `TraceRecord` object to begin the recording process.",
			"cellName": "Handle Start Trace Command - cmd-tracing.cpp:L234-239",
			"cellId": "2782195b-68d7-41dc-9fa4-247e256cab9d",
			"visible": true,
			"startLine": 234,
			"endLine": 239,
			"parentCellId": "b23dc46d-f8ba-437a-9906-3b8abc585040",
			"parentPath": "src/dbg/commands/cmd-tracing.cpp",
			"simSteps": [
				{
					"simulationKey": "How execution tracing works",
					"simStepId": "f73b0031-4cdf-428f-82a9-345d3e43ebb4"
				}
			]
		},
		"21f5a358-3632-41ef-a9c7-1ed812403fe0": {
			"path": "21f5a358-3632-41ef-a9c7-1ed812403fe0",
			"fileName": "21f5a358-3632-41ef-a9c7-1ed812403fe0",
			"cellName": "Initialize Trace File and State - TraceRecord.cpp:L486-561",
			"cellId": "21f5a358-3632-41ef-a9c7-1ed812403fe0",
			"visible": true,
			"parentCellId": "47254176-86e5-4ae6-b343-1dd769cbe5b2"
		},
		"src/dbg/TraceRecord.cpp-simstep-2d31b772-07ec-4df8-b286-2e1efe190535": {
			"path": "src/dbg/TraceRecord.cpp-simstep-2d31b772-07ec-4df8-b286-2e1efe190535",
			"fileName": "TraceRecord.cpp",
			"wiki": "The `TraceRecordManager::enableTraceRecording` method sets up the trace file and activates tracing mode. It creates the trace file, writes a JSON header with metadata (like architecture and debuggee hash), sets the internal `rtEnabled` flag to true, and immediately records the state of the current instruction to start the trace log.",
			"cellName": "Initialize Trace File and State - TraceRecord.cpp:L486-561",
			"cellId": "21f5a358-3632-41ef-a9c7-1ed812403fe0",
			"visible": true,
			"startLine": 486,
			"endLine": 561,
			"parentCellId": "47254176-86e5-4ae6-b343-1dd769cbe5b2",
			"parentPath": "src/dbg/TraceRecord.cpp",
			"simSteps": [
				{
					"simulationKey": "How execution tracing works",
					"simStepId": "2d31b772-07ec-4df8-b286-2e1efe190535"
				}
			]
		},
		"2d5e1d90-6fd7-4bfe-99b4-6a170fdc19d9": {
			"path": "2d5e1d90-6fd7-4bfe-99b4-6a170fdc19d9",
			"fileName": "2d5e1d90-6fd7-4bfe-99b4-6a170fdc19d9",
			"cellName": "Execute Step Callback - debugger.cpp:L1303-1329",
			"cellId": "2d5e1d90-6fd7-4bfe-99b4-6a170fdc19d9",
			"visible": true,
			"parentCellId": "4cedaf68-408e-481a-8895-afcd92ae8b82"
		},
		"src/dbg/debugger.cpp-simstep-a9b704f8-7e7c-4783-8ffa-f21f49eee210": {
			"path": "src/dbg/debugger.cpp-simstep-a9b704f8-7e7c-4783-8ffa-f21f49eee210",
			"fileName": "debugger.cpp",
			"wiki": "When the debugger pauses after the step, the `cbStep` callback function is executed. This function is the central handler for a single-step event. It updates the GUI state and calls `dbgtraceexecute` to record the instruction that was just executed.",
			"cellName": "Execute Step Callback - debugger.cpp:L1303-1329",
			"cellId": "2d5e1d90-6fd7-4bfe-99b4-6a170fdc19d9",
			"visible": true,
			"startLine": 1303,
			"endLine": 1329,
			"parentCellId": "4cedaf68-408e-481a-8895-afcd92ae8b82",
			"parentPath": "src/dbg/debugger.cpp",
			"simSteps": [
				{
					"simulationKey": "How execution tracing works",
					"simStepId": "a9b704f8-7e7c-4783-8ffa-f21f49eee210"
				}
			]
		},
		"90f5a346-2b51-4e8a-bbd2-66f8b093698d": {
			"path": "90f5a346-2b51-4e8a-bbd2-66f8b093698d",
			"fileName": "90f5a346-2b51-4e8a-bbd2-66f8b093698d",
			"cellName": "Process and Record Trace Data - TraceRecord.cpp:L706-740",
			"cellId": "90f5a346-2b51-4e8a-bbd2-66f8b093698d",
			"visible": true,
			"parentCellId": "47254176-86e5-4ae6-b343-1dd769cbe5b2"
		},
		"src/dbg/TraceRecord.cpp-simstep-84aab721-9b66-4311-9938-4a99389d0880": {
			"path": "src/dbg/TraceRecord.cpp-simstep-84aab721-9b66-4311-9938-4a99389d0880",
			"fileName": "TraceRecord.cpp",
			"wiki": "The `dbgtraceexecute` function orchestrates the recording. It checks if trace recording is enabled. If so, it reads the instruction from memory, disassembles it, and calls `TraceExecuteRecord` to perform the detailed logging of the execution state.",
			"cellName": "Process and Record Trace Data - TraceRecord.cpp:L706-740",
			"cellId": "90f5a346-2b51-4e8a-bbd2-66f8b093698d",
			"visible": true,
			"startLine": 706,
			"endLine": 740,
			"parentCellId": "47254176-86e5-4ae6-b343-1dd769cbe5b2",
			"parentPath": "src/dbg/TraceRecord.cpp",
			"simSteps": [
				{
					"simulationKey": "How execution tracing works",
					"simStepId": "84aab721-9b66-4311-9938-4a99389d0880"
				}
			]
		},
		"fe8a96b9-8d95-4a8f-b531-b040d671732f": {
			"path": "fe8a96b9-8d95-4a8f-b531-b040d671732f",
			"fileName": "fe8a96b9-8d95-4a8f-b531-b040d671732f",
			"cellName": "Write Delta-Compressed State to File - TraceRecord.cpp:L251-430",
			"cellId": "fe8a96b9-8d95-4a8f-b531-b040d671732f",
			"visible": true,
			"parentCellId": "47254176-86e5-4ae6-b343-1dd769cbe5b2"
		},
		"src/dbg/TraceRecord.cpp-simstep-85d78f8c-b21a-4622-9a4d-52137554b9c7": {
			"path": "src/dbg/TraceRecord.cpp-simstep-85d78f8c-b21a-4622-9a4d-52137554b9c7",
			"fileName": "TraceRecord.cpp",
			"wiki": "`TraceExecuteRecord` captures the full CPU context (registers, flags), compares it with the previous state to find changes (delta compression), serializes this information into a compact binary format, and writes the resulting buffer to the trace file.",
			"cellName": "Write Delta-Compressed State to File - TraceRecord.cpp:L251-430",
			"cellId": "fe8a96b9-8d95-4a8f-b531-b040d671732f",
			"visible": true,
			"startLine": 251,
			"endLine": 430,
			"parentCellId": "47254176-86e5-4ae6-b343-1dd769cbe5b2",
			"parentPath": "src/dbg/TraceRecord.cpp",
			"simSteps": [
				{
					"simulationKey": "How execution tracing works",
					"simStepId": "85d78f8c-b21a-4622-9a4d-52137554b9c7"
				}
			]
		},
		"56098996-2f19-4ea9-be9d-1dd9eb18626c": {
