		"4c29a848-07d1-42a8-9087-11a17b0f83b1": {
			"path": "4c29a848-07d1-42a8-9087-11a17b0f83b1",
			"fileName": "4c29a848-07d1-42a8-9087-11a17b0f83b1",
			"cellName": "Exception Handler Entry Point - debugger.cpp:L2093-2101",
			"cellId": "4c29a848-07d1-42a8-9087-11a17b0f83b1",
			"visible": true,
			"parentCellId": "4cedaf68-408e-481a-8895-afcd92ae8b82"
		},
		"src/dbg/debugger.cpp-simstep-398890fe-1ab6-471e-8896-62e5403fab54": {
			"path": "src/dbg/debugger.cpp-simstep-398890fe-1ab6-471e-8896-62e5403fab54",
			"fileName": "debugger.cpp",
			"wiki": "The debug loop receives the debug event and calls `cbException`, the main handler for all exceptions. It updates the last exception info and notifies the GUI.",
			"cellName": "Exception Handler Entry Point - debugger.cpp:L2093-2101",
			"cellId": "4c29a848-07d1-42a8-9087-11a17b0f83b1",
			"visible": true,
			"startLine": 2093,
			"endLine": 2101,
			"parentCellId": "4cedaf68-408e-481a-8895-afcd92ae8b82",
			"parentPath": "src/dbg/debugger.cpp",
			"simSteps": [
				{
					"simulationKey": "How exception handling works",
					"simStepId": "398890fe-1ab6-471e-8896-62e5403fab54"
				}
			]
		},
		"bca6f3a2-05bd-470d-84aa-9485f96ece5a": {
			"path": "bca6f3a2-05bd-470d-84aa-9485f96ece5a",
			"fileName": "bca6f3a2-05bd-470d-84aa-9485f96ece5a",
			"cellName": "Custom Breakpoint Path vs. Filter Path - debugger.cpp:L2104-2114",
			"cellId": "bca6f3a2-05bd-470d-84aa-9485f96ece5a",
			"visible": true,
			"parentCellId": "4cedaf68-408e-481a-8895-afcd92ae8b82"
		},
		"src/dbg/debugger.cpp-simstep-ec9e0cb8-797e-4531-9671-b7523877da7f": {
			"path": "src/dbg/debugger.cpp-simstep-ec9e0cb8-797e-4531-9671-b7523877da7f",
			"fileName": "debugger.cpp",
			"wiki": "The execution path diverges here. If a custom exception breakpoint (`SetExceptionBPX`) exists for the exception code, `cbGenericBreakpoint` is called to handle it like a normal breakpoint. If not, the debugger proceeds to check the general exception filters defined in the settings.",
			"cellName": "Custom Breakpoint Path vs. Filter Path - debugger.cpp:L2104-2114",
			"cellId": "bca6f3a2-05bd-470d-84aa-9485f96ece5a",
			"visible": true,
			"startLine": 2104,
			"endLine": 2114,
			"parentCellId": "4cedaf68-408e-481a-8895-afcd92ae8b82",
			"parentPath": "src/dbg/debugger.cpp",
			"simSteps": [
				{
					"simulationKey": "How exception handling works",
					"simStepId": "ec9e0cb8-797e-4531-9671-b7523877da7f"
				}
			]
		},
		"ed7560a7-b1bd-459c-ab2b-647898749e82": {
			"path": "ed7560a7-b1bd-459c-ab2b-647898749e82",
			"fileName": "ed7560a7-b1bd-459c-ab2b-647898749e82",
			"cellName": "Apply Exception Filter Rules - debugger.cpp:L2145-2171",
			"cellId": "ed7560a7-b1bd-459c-ab2b-647898749e82",
			"visible": true,
			"parentCellId": "4cedaf68-408e-481a-8895-afcd92ae8b82"
		},
		"src/dbg/debugger.cpp-simstep-fcc30b21-c611-402f-836d-bf73d8dab948": {
			"path": "src/dbg/debugger.cpp-simstep-fcc30b21-c611-402f-836d-bf73d8dab948",
			"fileName": "debugger.cpp",
			"wiki": "The `dbggetexceptionfilter` function returns the appropriate filter. The `cbException` function then uses this filter to decide whether to break, whether to log, and how to continue (pass the exception to the debuggee or swallow it).",
			"cellName": "Apply Exception Filter Rules - debugger.cpp:L2145-2171",
			"cellId": "ed7560a7-b1bd-459c-ab2b-647898749e82",
			"visible": true,
			"startLine": 2145,
			"endLine": 2171,
			"parentCellId": "4cedaf68-408e-481a-8895-afcd92ae8b82",
			"parentPath": "src/dbg/debugger.cpp",
			"simSteps": [
				{
					"simulationKey": "How exception handling works",
					"simStepId": "fcc30b21-c611-402f-836d-bf73d8dab948"
				}
			]
		},
		"7446b2c4-b36e-4ee3-9b58-59c2db9aa360": {
			"path": "7446b2c4-b36e-4ee3-9b58-59c2db9aa360",
			"fileName": "7446b2c4-b36e-4ee3-9b58-59c2db9aa360",
			"cellName": "Pause Debugger and Wait for User - debugger.cpp:L2173-2185",
			"cellId": "7446b2c4-b36e-4ee3-9b58-59c2db9aa360",
			"visible": true,
			"parentCellId": "4cedaf68-408e-481a-8895-afcd92ae8b82"
		},
		"src/dbg/debugger.cpp-simstep-08ead610-8fe9-43db-8417-9fa04fd5669c": {
			"path": "src/dbg/debugger.cpp-simstep-08ead610-8fe9-43db-8417-9fa04fd5669c",
			"fileName": "debugger.cpp",
			"wiki": "If the filter settings determine that the debugger should break, the GUI is updated to a 'paused' state, the debug loop is locked, and the system waits for user interaction. Plugin callbacks for pausing and exceptions are fired.",
			"cellName": "Pause Debugger and Wait for User - debugger.cpp:L2173-2185",
			"cellId": "7446b2c4-b36e-4ee3-9b58-59c2db9aa360",
			"visible": true,
			"startLine": 2173,
			"endLine": 2185,
			"parentCellId": "4cedaf68-408e-481a-8895-afcd92ae8b82",
			"parentPath": "src/dbg/debugger.cpp",
			"simSteps": [
				{
					"simulationKey": "How exception handling works",
					"simStepId": "08ead610-8fe9-43db-8417-9fa04fd5669c"
				}
			]
		},
		"b6e16ad5-ecfa-49de-849f-71de65f8c872": {
			"path": "b6e16ad5-ecfa-49de-849f-71de65f8c872",
			"fileName": "b6e16ad5-ecfa-49de-849f-71de65f8c872",
			"cellName": "Enable 'Skip Exceptions' Flag - cmd-debug-control.cpp:L356-357",
			"cellId": "b6e16ad5-ecfa-49de-849f-71de65f8c872",
			"visible": true,
			"parentCellId": "110ba731-9074-4a40-a86e-74cc73f27d55"
		},
		"src/dbg/commands/cmd-debug-control.cpp-simstep-8fb57243-eff8-4afa-b455-99595000769d": {
			"path": "src/dbg/commands/cmd-debug-control.cpp-simstep-8fb57243-eff8-4afa-b455-99595000769d",
			"fileName": "cmd-debug-control.cpp",
			"wiki": "The `erun` command handler `cbDebugErun` calls `dbgsetskipexceptions(true)`. This sets an internal flag that will cause the `cbException` function to immediately return for any subsequent first-chance exceptions, effectively ignoring them.",
			"cellName": "Enable 'Skip Exceptions' Flag - cmd-debug-control.cpp:L356-357",
			"cellId": "b6e16ad5-ecfa-49de-849f-71de65f8c872",
			"visible": true,
			"startLine": 356,
			"endLine": 357,
			"parentCellId": "110ba731-9074-4a40-a86e-74cc73f27d55",
			"parentPath": "src/dbg/commands/cmd-debug-control.cpp",
			"simSteps": [
				{
					"simulationKey": "How exception handling works",
					"simStepId": "8fb57243-eff8-4afa-b455-99595000769d"
				}
			]
		},
		"6947b6d2-96c6-4b5b-93aa-e5d359423274": {
			"path": "6947b6d2-96c6-4b5b-93aa-e5d359423274",
			"fileName": "6947b6d2-96c6-4b5b-93aa-e5d359423274",
			"cellName": "Update Continue Status for Current Exception - cmd-debug-control.cpp:L433-446",
			"cellId": "6947b6d2-96c6-4b5b-93aa-e5d359423274",
			"visible": true,
			"parentCellId": "110ba731-9074-4a40-a86e-74cc73f27d55"
		},
		"src/dbg/commands/cmd-debug-control.cpp-simstep-60d60766-161f-4c8c-9a69-e0e9c6ac84f0": {
			"path": "src/dbg/commands/cmd-debug-control.cpp-simstep-60d60766-161f-4c8c-9a69-e0e9c6ac84f0",
			"fileName": "cmd-debug-control.cpp",
			"wiki": "The `cbDebugContinue` handler is executed. It calls `dbgsetcontinuestatus` again, overwriting the value set by the exception filter with the user's explicit choice (either `DBG_CONTINUE` or `DBG_EXCEPTION_NOT_HANDLED`). This alters the behavior when the debugger is eventually resumed.",
			"cellName": "Update Continue Status for Current Exception - cmd-debug-control.cpp:L433-446",
			"cellId": "6947b6d2-96c6-4b5b-93aa-e5d359423274",
			"visible": true,
			"startLine": 433,
			"endLine": 446,
			"parentCellId": "110ba731-9074-4a40-a86e-74cc73f27d55",
			"parentPath": "src/dbg/commands/cmd-debug-control.cpp",
			"simSteps": [
				{
					"simulationKey": "How exception handling works",
					"simStepId": "60d60766-161f-4c8c-9a69-e0e9c6ac84f0"
				}
			]
		},
		"e6750efd-78cd-4bed-ab03-e92ea59ea528": {
