		"How inspecting program state works": {
			"name": "How inspecting program state works",
			"simSteps": [
				{
					"simStepId": "0a1399a9-b30c-4a9f-84e5-60f34cf3c83c",
					"diagramNodeId": "aaafc0a9-b260-43f6-92ca-64748c4dca4a",
					"simStepLabel": "Debugger Paused: GUI Update Initiated",
					"simStepDescription": "When the debuggee pauses, the debugger core triggers a refresh of the user interface. This process starts in the bridge component, which calls individual update functions for different parts of the GUI, beginning with the register view.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/bridge/bridgemain.cpp",
						"startLine": "1694",
						"endLine": "1698",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"GuiUpdateRegisterView"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"debug_event\": \"pause\", \"reason\": \"breakpoint_hit\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "1b512bb2-5af7-4dda-a822-7383f7347748",
					"diagramNodeId": "6201be85-da45-4f6b-b260-690a9cab4445",
					"simStepLabel": "Send Register Update Message",
					"simStepDescription": "The `GuiUpdateRegisterView` function sends a `GUI_UPDATE_REGISTER_VIEW` message to the main GUI thread via `_gui_sendmessage`. This message signals that the register view needs to be refreshed with the new state of the debuggee.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/bridge/bridgemain.cpp",
						"startLine": "1697",
						"endLine": "1697",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"_gui_sendmessage",
							"GUI_UPDATE_REGISTER_VIEW"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"message_type\": \"GUI_UPDATE_REGISTER_VIEW\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"message_type\": \"GUI_UPDATE_REGISTER_VIEW\"}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "9d817ead-f677-494b-987d-9b12cfb5982c",
					"diagramNodeId": "a7a45aa5-81b1-4110-90f5-5d2788ed7abd",
					"simStepLabel": "Bridge Processes Message and Emits Signal",
					"simStepDescription": "The main GUI bridge receives the `GUI_UPDATE_REGISTER_VIEW` message. It processes this message and, to avoid overwhelming the UI with rapid updates, uses a throttling mechanism. It then emits a Qt signal, `updateRegisters()`, to notify the relevant UI components.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/gui/Src/Bridge/Bridge.cpp",
						"startLine": "117",
						"endLine": "119",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"doUpdate",
							"GUI_UPDATE_REGISTER_VIEW",
							"updateRegisters"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"message_type\": \"GUI_UPDATE_REGISTER_VIEW\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"qt_signal\": \"updateRegisters()\"}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "8b733116-ce11-4553-99f5-313a629b7631",
					"diagramNodeId": "dc1e8668-1a6e-4ab3-97ba-97c17248cda7",
					"simStepLabel": "Signal to CPURegistersView",
					"simStepDescription": "The `updateRegisters()` signal is propagated through Qt's signal-slot mechanism to the `CPURegistersView` component, which is responsible for displaying the CPU registers.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/gui/Src/Gui/CPURegistersView.cpp",
						"startLine": "17",
						"endLine": "17",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"updateRegistersSlot"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"qt_signal\": \"updateRegisters()\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"qt_signal\": \"updateRegisters()\"}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "4b7620fe-edfc-4066-ad83-e0fee68d4481",
					"diagramNodeId": "97f7adb1-6a2c-4a44-936f-fbdb045482e4",
					"simStepLabel": "Fetch Register Data",
					"simStepDescription": "The `updateRegistersSlot` in `CPURegistersView` is executed. It calls the `DbgGetRegDumpEx` function to request the complete register state from the debugger core.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/gui/Src/Gui/CPURegistersView.cpp",
						"startLine": "203",
						"endLine": "212",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"updateRegistersSlot",
							"DbgGetRegDumpEx"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"register_dump_request\": {}}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "1c526ff8-397a-432a-88a2-87bdb086251f",
					"diagramNodeId": "4445758f-e301-47b6-a715-faecfb554109",
					"simStepLabel": "Retrieve Thread Context from Debugger Core",
					"simStepDescription": "The `DbgGetRegDumpEx` call crosses the bridge into the debugger core. The core retrieves the full thread context, including general-purpose registers, flags, FPU/SSE registers, and debug registers.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/bridge/bridgemain.cpp",
						"startLine": "846",
						"endLine": "852",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"DbgGetRegDumpEx",
							"_dbg_getregdump"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"RAX\": \"0x7FF6B49D1000\", \"RBX\": \"0x0\", \"RCX\": \"0x1A29D8FD820\", \"RDX\": \"0x0\", \"RSP\": \"0x1A29D8FD738\", \"RBP\": \"0x1A29D8FD820\", \"RIP\": \"0x7FF958E4D9B4\", \"EFL\": \"0x246\"}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "e8c14476-191c-4307-abdb-b944b0751546",
					"diagramNodeId": "421f4f68-9407-47fb-9d47-14d673311c38",
					"simStepLabel": "Render Register View",
					"simStepDescription": "The `REGDUMP_AVX512` structure containing the register data is returned to `CPURegistersView`. The `setRegisters` method is then called to parse this structure and update the labels in the UI, highlighting any registers that have changed.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/gui/Src/Gui/CPURegistersView.cpp",
						"startLine": "209",
						"endLine": "211",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"setRegisters"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"RAX\": \"0x7FF6B49D1000\", \"RBX\": \"0x0\", \"RCX\": \"0x1A29D8FD820\", \"RDX\": \"0x0\", \"RSP\": \"0x1A29D8FD738\", \"RBP\": \"0x1A29D8FD820\", \"RIP\": \"0x7FF958E4D9B4\", \"EFL\": \"0x246\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "d823a60e-06fe-4184-905d-370be40c59f9",
					"diagramNodeId": "fdd601dd-4844-4457-9f52-24a3efbc6544",
					"simStepLabel": "Request Dump, Stack and Callstack Update",
					"simStepDescription": "Continuing the UI refresh process, the bridge sends messages to update the memory dump, stack, and call stack views.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/bridge/bridgemain.cpp",
						"startLine": "1877",
						"endLine": "1998",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"GuiUpdateDumpView",
							"GuiUpdateCallStack"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"message_type\": [\"GUI_UPDATE_DUMP_VIEW\", \"GUI_UPDATE_CALLSTACK\"]}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "d95fa17d-54cc-48f7-8fb0-d54ba9c91578",
					"diagramNodeId": "5f89b73b-b1c8-4126-8b4c-41012e6bf958",
					"simStepLabel": "Bridge Emits Update Signals for Dumps and Stack",
					"simStepDescription": "The bridge processes the `GUI_UPDATE_DUMP_VIEW` and `GUI_UPDATE_CALLSTACK` messages, emitting the corresponding `updateDump()` and `updateCallStack()` signals.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/gui/Src/Bridge/Bridge.cpp",
						"startLine": "129",
						"endLine": "155",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"GUI_UPDATE_DUMP_VIEW",
							"updateDump",
							"GUI_UPDATE_CALLSTACK",
							"updateCallStack"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"message_type\": [\"GUI_UPDATE_DUMP_VIEW\", \"GUI_UPDATE_CALLSTACK\"]}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"qt_signal\": [\"updateDump()\", \"updateCallStack()\"]}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "9b825ff9-f323-410e-a4a9-ce1899d55bea",
					"diagramNodeId": "ffc09647-31e5-4177-89cd-002e4efac857",
					"simStepLabel": "Signals Propagated to UI Views",
					"simStepDescription": "The `updateDump()` signal is received by `CPUMultiDump` (for memory views) and `CPUStack`. The `updateCallStack()` signal is received by the `CallStackView` and also implicitly handled by `CPUStack`'s update logic.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/gui/Src/Gui/CPUStack.cpp",
						"startLine": "54",
						"endLine": "54",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"updateDump"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"qt_signal\": [\"updateDump()\", \"updateCallStack()\"]}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"qt_signal\": [\"updateDump()\", \"updateCallStack()\"]}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "0967cde1-1b11-4704-9e74-bd8ccd84b9cb",
					"diagramNodeId": "d4e98c5b-dcde-4c5c-9ea2-631033010b03",
					"simStepLabel": "Fetch and Render Stack and Memory Dumps",
					"simStepDescription": "The `CPUStack::updateSlot` is triggered, which calls `DbgFunctions()->GetCallStack()` to retrieve call stack frames. Both `CPUStack` and `CPUDump` then read memory from the debuggee using their internal `MemoryPage` objects to refresh their content.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/gui/Src/Gui/CPUStack.cpp",
						"startLine": "574",
						"endLine": "602",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"updateSlot",
							"DbgFunctions()->GetCallStack",
							"mCallstack"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"call_stack_frames\": [{\"addr\": \"0x...\"}, {\"addr\": \"0x...\"}], \"memory_content\": \"00 11 22 ...\"}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "917041af-7f7e-46e0-8be1-35b9cbbc831c",
					"diagramNodeId": "8f74d48c-c078-4b81-9ceb-4639b4d8c17e",
					"simStepLabel": "Request Watch View Update",
					"simStepDescription": "The final part of the state inspection update is refreshing the Watch view. The bridge calls `GuiUpdateWatchView`.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/bridge/bridgemain.cpp",
						"startLine": "1883",
						"endLine": "1883",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"GuiUpdateWatchView"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"message_type\": \"GUI_UPDATE_WATCH_VIEW\"}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "aa717f54-e0bb-411f-96b5-9cf402fbec68",
					"diagramNodeId": "8fedaaf0-f232-4458-bd98-24c2594303ea",
					"simStepLabel": "Bridge Emits `updateWatch()` Signal",
					"simStepDescription": "The bridge receives the `GUI_UPDATE_WATCH_VIEW` message, processes it, and emits the `updateWatch()` Qt signal.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/gui/Src/Bridge/Bridge.cpp",
						"startLine": "169",
						"endLine": "171",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"GUI_UPDATE_WATCH_VIEW",
							"updateWatch"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"message_type\": \"GUI_UPDATE_WATCH_VIEW\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"qt_signal\": \"updateWatch()\"}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "7bdaa568-72e2-4f70-b8e0-6f45659d53b9",
					"diagramNodeId": "1da55565-5636-4469-961c-84ec0ddc48a3",
					"simStepLabel": "Signal to WatchView",
					"simStepDescription": "The `updateWatch()` signal is propagated to the `WatchView` component.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/gui/Src/Gui/WatchView.cpp",
						"startLine": "17",
						"endLine": "17",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"updateWatch"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"qt_signal\": \"updateWatch()\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"qt_signal\": \"updateWatch()\"}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "ca971f33-2245-4f8e-a874-18e5657f46f4",
					"diagramNodeId": "c3341733-92e8-4453-8706-ed62e65aa57d",
					"simStepLabel": "Fetch Watch List and Evaluate Expressions",
					"simStepDescription": "The `WatchView::updateWatch` slot is executed. It calls `DbgGetWatchList` to retrieve the list of watched expressions and their current values.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/gui/Src/Gui/WatchView.cpp",
						"startLine": "25",
						"endLine": "35",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"updateWatch",
							"DbgGetWatchList"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"watch_list_request\": {}}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "3027d998-460b-42c8-9af4-5abcb28b4870",
					"diagramNodeId": "6e222bdf-ef72-4098-9361-2425ccb7bd16",
					"simStepLabel": "Evaluate Expressions in Debugger Core",
					"simStepDescription": "The call to `DbgGetWatchList` is handled by the debugger core. It iterates through each watch expression, evaluates it by parsing and looking up register values and memory, and computes the final result.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/dbg/watch.cpp",
						"startLine": "289",
						"endLine": "293",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"WatchGetList"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"watch_list_request\": {}}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"watches\": [{\"name\": \"myVar\", \"expression\": \"[rsp+8]\", \"value\": \"0x7FF958E4D9B4\", \"type\": \"UINT\"}]}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "fd48a3c9-31a5-4547-8fc0-142cb9056834",
					"diagramNodeId": "31cb3666-8e52-4eb4-8185-209f1bf73650",
					"simStepLabel": "Render Watch View",
					"simStepDescription": "The list of evaluated watch expressions (`WATCHINFO`) is returned to `WatchView`. The view then iterates through the list and updates the table cells with the new names, expressions, and values, completing the state inspection update.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/gui/Src/Gui/WatchView.cpp",
						"startLine": "38",
						"endLine": "128",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"WatchList",
							"setCellContent"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"watches\": [{\"name\": \"myVar\", \"expression\": \"[rsp+8]\", \"value\": \"0x7FF958E4D9B4\", \"type\": \"UINT\"}]}",
					"outputDataExample": "{}"
				}
			],
			"description": "<ul><li>- When the debuggee is paused, users can inspect its complete state</li><li>- The CPU View is the central hub, displaying general-purpose registers (EAX, RAX, etc</li><li>), flags, FPU/SSE registers, the call stack, and memory dumps</li><li>- <code>CPURegistersView</li><li>cpp</code> handles fetching and displaying register values from the <code>REGDUMP</code> structure provided by the debugger core</li><li>- The Dump and Stack views (<code>CPUMultiDump</li><li>cpp</code>, <code>CPUStack</li><li>cpp</code>) read memory directly from the debuggee to display its contents</li><li>- The Watch view (<code>WatchView</li><li>cpp</code>) allows users to monitor the value of arbitrary expressions, which are re-evaluated each time the debugger pauses</li></ul>",
			"simulationNodesAndEdges": {
				"aaafc0a9-b260-43f6-92ca-64748c4dca4a": {
