		"How code analysis and navigation works": {
			"name": "How code analysis and navigation works",
			"simSteps": [
				{
					"simStepId": "f3fd3323-ca77-43f8-8332-a44ca4ebea30",
					"diagramNodeId": "b8dab04d-9813-4d45-95eb-34ca981be919",
					"simStepLabel": "Start: Display Disassembly in Graph View",
					"simStepDescription": "The process begins when the DisassemblerGraphView needs to display a control flow graph. It iterates through the basic blocks and instructions provided by the backend's control flow analysis. For each instruction's machine code, it calls `disasm.DisassembleAt` to get a structured and tokenized representation for rendering.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/gui/Src/Gui/DisassemblerGraphView.cpp",
						"startLine": "2058",
						"endLine": "2058",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"disasm.DisassembleAt",
							"nodeInstr",
							"addr"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"address\": \"0x140001000\", \"machine_code\": \"55488bec4883ec20\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"Instruction_t\": {\"rva\": 256, \"length\": 4, \"instStr\": \"push rbp\", \"tokens\": [{\"type\": \"MnemonicPushPop\", \"text\": \"push\"}, {\"type\": \"Space\", \"text\": \" \"}, {\"type\": \"GeneralRegister\", \"text\": \"rbp\"}]}}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "f327922a-e01d-4f43-bb80-f683677a3b1f",
					"diagramNodeId": "eb671855-5a6a-4f98-9ad4-19381f738e8b",
					"simStepLabel": "Data Flow: Pass Raw Instruction to QZydis",
					"simStepDescription": "The raw machine code bytes and the instruction's virtual address are passed from the graph view to the `QZydis` wrapper, which orchestrates the disassembly and tokenization process.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/gui/Src/Gui/DisassemblerGraphView.cpp",
						"startLine": "2058",
						"endLine": "2058",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"disasm.DisassembleAt"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"address\": \"0x140001000\", \"data\": \"55488bec4883ec20\", \"size\": 16}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"address\": \"0x140001000\", \"data\": \"55488bec4883ec20\", \"size\": 16}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "265caf94-f778-48fc-aff8-69cf52c08991",
					"diagramNodeId": "00fcf01c-98b2-43cd-b77d-d6b71565d1dd",
					"simStepLabel": "Tokenization: QZydis Invokes ZydisTokenizer",
					"simStepDescription": "`QZydis` is a Qt-level wrapper that delegates the tokenization process to its internal `ZydisTokenizer` instance. The tokenizer's role is to convert raw instruction bytes into a series of styled tokens for syntax highlighting.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/gui/Src/Disassembler/QZydis.cpp",
						"startLine": "200",
						"endLine": "200",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"mTokenizer.Tokenize"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"address\": \"0x140001000\", \"data\": \"55488bec4883ec20\", \"size\": 16}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"InstructionToken\": {\"tokens\": [{\"type\": \"MnemonicPushPop\", \"text\": \"push\"}, {\"type\": \"Space\", \"text\": \" \"}, {\"type\": \"GeneralRegister\", \"text\": \"rbp\"}]}}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "ea6aaf91-6c44-4a9f-be4b-08c8ab789fbe",
					"diagramNodeId": "d842f0f9-6415-4f16-b8f4-dee11c777160",
					"simStepLabel": "Data Flow: Pass Raw Instruction to Tokenizer",
					"simStepDescription": "The raw instruction bytes and address are passed down to the `ZydisTokenizer` for low-level disassembly and conversion into tokens.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/gui/Src/Disassembler/QZydis.cpp",
						"startLine": "200",
						"endLine": "200",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"mTokenizer.Tokenize"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"address\": \"0x140001000\", \"data\": \"55488bec4883ec20\", \"size\": 16}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"address\": \"0x140001000\", \"data\": \"55488bec4883ec20\", \"size\": 16}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "831619c1-3251-4112-b846-517140a635c3",
					"diagramNodeId": "f4af227c-f71f-4748-a20e-b12b64376074",
					"simStepLabel": "Disassembly: ZydisTokenizer uses Zydis Wrapper",
					"simStepDescription": "The tokenizer uses its `Zydis` member object, a C++ wrapper around the core Zydis library, to perform the actual machine code disassembly. It calls `DisassembleSafe` which handles potential read errors.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/gui/Src/Disassembler/ZydisTokenizer.cpp",
						"startLine": "136",
						"endLine": "136",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"mZydis.DisassembleSafe"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"address\": \"0x140001000\", \"data\": \"55488bec4883ec20\", \"size\": 16}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"mSuccess\": true, \"mInstr\": {\"info\": {\"mnemonic\": \"ZYDIS_MNEMONIC_PUSH\", \"length\": 1}, \"operands\": [...]}}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "b8edabc2-2ee5-4d0f-88f5-5ccf8e35cb8d",
					"diagramNodeId": "a6feb214-848c-47bc-8120-dbb3e4d07fe2",
					"simStepLabel": "Data Flow: Pass Raw Instruction to Zydis Wrapper",
					"simStepDescription": "The raw instruction bytes and address are passed to the final C++ wrapper before calling the Zydis C library.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/gui/Src/Disassembler/ZydisTokenizer.cpp",
						"startLine": "136",
						"endLine": "136",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"mZydis.DisassembleSafe"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"address\": \"0x140001000\", \"data\": \"55488bec4883ec20\", \"size\": 16}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"address\": \"0x140001000\", \"data\": \"55488bec4883ec20\", \"size\": 16}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "58f5b061-cc33-4e36-a39f-57bdae025b12",
					"diagramNodeId": "7135837f-6e40-4848-aaaf-fac4821004df",
					"simStepLabel": "Core Disassembly: Zydis Library Decoding and Formatting",
					"simStepDescription": "The `Zydis` wrapper calls `ZydisDecoderDecodeFull` to parse the machine code into a structured `ZydisDecodedInstruction`. It then uses `ZydisFormatterFormatInstruction` to get a human-readable text representation. Finally, it post-processes operands, for instance, calculating absolute addresses for relative operands using `ZydisCalcAbsoluteAddress`.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/zydis_wrapper/zydis_wrapper.cpp",
						"startLine": "91",
						"endLine": "118",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"ZydisDecoderDecodeFull",
							"ZydisFormatterFormatInstruction",
							"ZydisCalcAbsoluteAddress"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"address\": \"0x140001000\", \"data\": \"55488bec4883ec20\", \"size\": 16}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"mInstr.info\": {\"mnemonic\": \"ZYDIS_MNEMONIC_PUSH\"}, \"mInstrText\": \"push rbp\"}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "994aad26-968e-4cdc-a7c4-1b30e42306da",
					"diagramNodeId": "f5af3f2a-e47e-42ec-a10a-a134dacf232c",
					"simStepLabel": "Data Flow: Return Decoded Instruction",
					"simStepDescription": "The disassembled instruction, now in a structured and string format, is returned from the `Zydis` wrapper back to the `ZydisTokenizer` for further processing.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/zydis_wrapper/zydis_wrapper.cpp",
						"startLine": "129",
						"endLine": "130",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"mSuccess"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"mSuccess\": true, \"mInstr\": {\"info\": {\"mnemonic\": \"ZYDIS_MNEMONIC_PUSH\"}, \"operands\": [...]}, \"mInstrText\": \"push rbp\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"mSuccess\": true, \"mInstr\": {\"info\": {\"mnemonic\": \"ZYDIS_MNEMONIC_PUSH\"}, \"operands\": [...]}, \"mInstrText\": \"push rbp\"}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "fc56aef9-cc34-4bf9-8c78-bef6de54d8a7",
					"diagramNodeId": "c5eba0d7-5b22-4d77-8f0a-dc79aef3c358",
					"simStepLabel": "Token Generation: ZydisTokenizer Creates Tokens",
					"simStepDescription": "The `ZydisTokenizer` processes the results from the `Zydis` wrapper. It breaks down the instruction into logical parts (prefixes, mnemonic, operands) and creates a series of `SingleToken` objects, assigning a type to each for syntax highlighting.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/gui/Src/Disassembler/ZydisTokenizer.cpp",
						"startLine": "139",
						"endLine": "171",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"tokenizePrefix",
							"tokenizeMnemonic",
							"tokenizeOperand"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"mInstr.info\": {\"mnemonic\": \"ZYDIS_MNEMONIC_PUSH\"}, \"operands\": [...]}}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"mInst.tokens\": [{\"type\": \"MnemonicPushPop\", \"text\": \"push\"}, {\"type\": \"Space\", \"text\": \" \"}, {\"type\": \"GeneralRegister\", \"text\": \"rbp\"}]}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "b1d94020-a52a-43ae-ae64-4ee0f1636074",
					"diagramNodeId": "f97c3b4d-9ae0-47ea-bf18-07f5ed283f93",
					"simStepLabel": "Data Flow: Return Final Instruction_t Object",
					"simStepDescription": "The fully analyzed and tokenized instruction, encapsulated in an `Instruction_t` object, is returned to the `DisassemblerGraphView`.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/gui/Src/Disassembler/QZydis.cpp",
						"startLine": "309",
						"endLine": "310",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"inst"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"Instruction_t\": {\"rva\": 256, \"length\": 4, \"instStr\": \"push rbp\", \"tokens\": [...]}}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"Instruction_t\": {\"rva\": 256, \"length\": 4, \"instStr\": \"push rbp\", \"tokens\": [...]}}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "87c61a43-5851-46ca-9d2d-2daf42c7b7ad",
					"diagramNodeId": "44c6ae39-15af-411d-8c5c-e81ee2aab945",
					"simStepLabel": "Final Step: Rendering Instruction Text",
					"simStepDescription": "The `DisassemblerGraphView` receives the `Instruction_t` object. It then converts the list of tokens into a `RichTextPainter::List`, which contains all necessary information (text, color, background) to render the syntax-highlighted instruction inside a graph node during the `paintEvent`.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/gui/Src/Gui/DisassemblerGraphView.cpp",
						"startLine": "2061",
						"endLine": "2116",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"ZydisTokenizer::TokenToRichText",
							"instr.text.addLine"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"Instruction_t\": {\"rva\": 256, \"length\": 4, \"instStr\": \"push rbp\", \"tokens\": [...]}}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"richText\": [{\"text\": \"push\", \"textColor\": \"#0000ff\"}, {\"text\": \" \"}, {\"text\": \"rbp\", \"textColor\": \"#ff0000\"}]}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "662e27fe-7d03-48aa-af28-c449663eafd8",
					"diagramNodeId": "b953549f-9b01-4148-aaef-2e93353313e9",
					"simStepLabel": "Control Flow: Triggering Graph Layout",
					"simStepDescription": "After processing all instructions for all nodes in the graph, the view proceeds to calculate the layout and render the entire function graph.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/gui/Src/Gui/DisassemblerGraphView.cpp",
						"startLine": "2134",
						"endLine": "2134",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"renderFunction"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"analysis\": {\"entry\": \"0x140001000\", \"functions\": [...]}}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"analysis\": {\"entry\": \"0x140001000\", \"functions\": [...]}}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "3a5b1fc1-d9ee-4086-b230-8ec4479e12af",
					"diagramNodeId": "d6b1f638-e50d-402f-b3b3-ba23efee43d6",
					"simStepLabel": "Graph Layout Calculation",
					"simStepDescription": "The `renderFunction` orchestrates the entire graph layout process. It first computes the relative positions of nodes (`computeGraphLayout`), then determines the paths for the edges connecting them (`routeEdge`), calculates the final pixel coordinates for all elements, and schedules a repaint of the viewport.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/gui/Src/Gui/DisassemblerGraphView.cpp",
						"startLine": "1540",
						"endLine": "1895",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"computeGraphLayout",
							"routeEdge",
							"viewport()->update"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"function\": {\"entry\": \"0x140001000\", \"blocks\": [...]}}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"blocks\": {\"0x140001000\": {\"x\": 100, \"y\": 50, \"width\": 250, \"height\": 80}}}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "98963bab-a137-49f8-bafa-bdd87471e0ea",
					"diagramNodeId": "2cf1e812-bd1c-480c-9cbf-c536babd0740",
					"simStepLabel": "Event: Qt Paint Event",
					"simStepDescription": "The call to `viewport()->update()` enqueues a paint event in the Qt event loop, which will eventually cause the `paintEvent` handler to be executed.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/gui/Src/Gui/DisassemblerGraphView.cpp",
						"startLine": "1893",
						"endLine": "1893",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"this->viewport()->update"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{}",
					"outputDataExample": "{}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "a1f04f9a-0450-4645-a876-a2fdac12c2b7",
					"diagramNodeId": "e30271a9-cf3c-4685-ba83-b126bb4dfeec",
					"simStepLabel": "Graph Rendering",
					"simStepDescription": "The `paintEvent` handler is executed by the GUI framework. It uses a `QPainter` object to draw the graph's nodes, edges, and the disassembled instruction text (which was prepared in the previous flow) onto the viewport widget, making the control flow graph visible to the user.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/gui/Src/Gui/DisassemblerGraphView.cpp",
						"startLine": "811",
						"endLine": "857",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"paintEvent",
							"paintNormal",
							"paintZoom"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"paintEvent\": {}}",
					"outputDataExample": "null"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "a3ecd2fb-c465-43f1-973b-d5e07f230605",
					"diagramNodeId": "dc728435-9eea-45e4-84e0-366606976ded",
					"simStepLabel": "User Action: Double-Click to Navigate",
					"simStepDescription": "A user double-clicks a branch instruction (like a JMP or CALL) in the disassembly view to navigate to its destination.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/gui/Src/Gui/DisassemblerGraphView.cpp",
						"startLine": "1198",
						"endLine": "1214",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"mouseDoubleClickEvent"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"event\": \"QMouseDoubleClickEvent\", \"instruction_address\": \"0x140001050\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"event\": \"QMouseDoubleClickEvent\", \"instruction_address\": \"0x140001050\"}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "8141a50a-9f15-4591-80ba-48f75191243b",
					"diagramNodeId": "6b16f6f3-79aa-440a-a603-10e6c8923238",
					"simStepLabel": "Navigation Command Execution",
					"simStepDescription": "The double-click event handler constructs and executes a `graph dis.branchdest(...)` command. This command instructs the debugger to resolve the branch destination of the specified instruction and then redraw the graph at that new address.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/gui/Src/Gui/DisassemblerGraphView.cpp",
						"startLine": "1212",
						"endLine": "1212",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"DbgCmdExec",
							"dis.branchdest"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"instruction_address\": \"0x140001050\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"command\": \"graph 0x1400010A0, silent\"}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "b795d219-7ac3-41cf-b819-666476a9bfa3",
					"diagramNodeId": "094057b3-393c-43b1-857d-90163cf2b6d3",
					"simStepLabel": "Data Flow: Resolve Branch Destination Request",
					"simStepDescription": "The `dis.branchdest` part of the command triggers a call to the backend to determine the target address of the branch instruction.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/dbg/_exports.cpp",
						"startLine": "801",
						"endLine": "801",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"_dbg_getbranchdestination"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"address\": \"0x140001050\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"address\": \"0x140001050\"}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "1702281e-39ff-4eb8-a093-6aa0503b3e12",
					"diagramNodeId": "b23655ae-ab6d-459e-b3ce-5a26a4c4ec16",
					"simStepLabel": "Backend: Branch Destination Resolution",
					"simStepDescription": "The `_dbg_getbranchdestination` function reads the instruction bytes, disassembles them using Zydis, and if it's a branch, resolves the destination. It can handle direct jumps (immediates), indirect jumps via registers, and memory-based jumps, using the current register context if necessary.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/dbg/_exports.cpp",
						"startLine": "801",
						"endLine": "893",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"zydis.Disassemble",
							"zydis.IsBranchType",
							"zydis.ResolveOpValue"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"address\": \"0x140001050\", \"bytes\": \"e84b000000\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"destination\": \"0x1400010A0\"}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "fa569d14-a5be-4e55-b171-5d93eba086b4",
					"diagramNodeId": "629694d3-6df9-4cf9-af40-60e8944be539",
					"simStepLabel": "Control Flow: Re-load Graph at New Address",
					"simStepDescription": "The resolved destination address is used to execute the `graph` command. This sends a request back to the `DisassemblerGraphView` to load and render the control flow graph for the new function or location, effectively restarting the process from the graph loading step.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/gui/Src/Gui/DisassemblerGraphView.cpp",
						"startLine": "2137",
						"endLine": "2157",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"loadGraphSlot"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"command\": \"graph 0x1400010A0\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"command\": \"graph 0x1400010A0\"}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "fc71c6c5-e506-4996-8f7d-b064dbdca723",
					"diagramNodeId": "a5461ffd-c5c7-47f3-bf4a-35c97e853e71",
					"simStepLabel": "User Action: Request Cross-References",
					"simStepDescription": "The user right-clicks an instruction in the disassembly or graph view and selects the 'Xrefs...' option from the context menu to find all references to the selected address.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/gui/Src/Gui/DisassemblerGraphView.cpp",
						"startLine": "2613",
						"endLine": "2632",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"xrefSlot"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"event\": \"QContextMenuEvent\", \"address\": \"0x140001000\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "null"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "1654e2cc-d10a-4edc-a6f9-4401409bf58c",
					"diagramNodeId": "e390f0a4-afe3-4934-9c13-0f693d0d10f4",
					"simStepLabel": "Data Flow: Request X-Refs from Backend",
					"simStepDescription": "A call is made to the debugger backend function `DbgXrefGet`, passing the address for which to find cross-references.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/gui/Src/Gui/DisassemblerGraphView.cpp",
						"startLine": "2621",
						"endLine": "2621",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"DbgXrefGet"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"address\": \"0x140001000\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"address\": \"0x140001000\"}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "705d4f35-af17-4753-b8db-6889be289dc9",
					"diagramNodeId": "80dfedcd-fa3a-4bc1-85b6-ad7c932e3f32",
					"simStepLabel": "Backend: X-Ref Analysis",
					"simStepDescription": "The `DbgXrefGet` function (abstracted, as `xrefs.cpp` is not provided) queries the debugger's internal cross-reference database. This database, built during analysis passes, stores all known locations that refer to any given address, including calls, jumps, and data references.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/dbg/_exports.cpp",
						"startLine": "102",
						"endLine": "889",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"_dbg_xrefget"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"address\": \"0x140001000\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"XREF_INFO\": {\"refcount\": 2, \"references\": [{\"addr\": \"0x14000104B\"}, {\"addr\": \"0x140001082\"}]}}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "1da8da7f-1e05-4edf-a7b0-c5edd378d558",
					"diagramNodeId": "c8b71107-f4d4-42f5-ba12-5767eb3ab3b2",
					"simStepLabel": "Data Flow: Return X-Ref Results",
					"simStepDescription": "The backend returns a list of cross-references to the GUI thread.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/gui/Src/Gui/DisassemblerGraphView.cpp",
						"startLine": "2621",
						"endLine": "2621",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"mXrefInfo"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"XREF_INFO\": {\"refcount\": 2, \"references\": [{\"addr\": \"0x14000104B\"}, {\"addr\": \"0x140001082\"}]}}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"XREF_INFO\": {\"refcount\": 2, \"references\": [{\"addr\": \"0x14000104B\"}, {\"addr\": \"0x140001082\"}]}}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "65f43ea7-a68a-4e89-8ad7-c74225c9b979",
					"diagramNodeId": "d10aca7d-cd07-44f4-be6e-3649089158fd",
					"simStepLabel": "Final Step: Display X-Ref Dialog",
					"simStepDescription": "If any cross-references were found, the `xrefSlot` creates and displays an `XrefBrowseDialog`, populating it with the list of addresses that refer to the target. The user can then double-click an entry in this dialog to navigate to that location.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/gui/Src/Gui/DisassemblerGraphView.cpp",
						"startLine": "2626",
						"endLine": "2631",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"mXrefDlg"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"mXrefInfo\": {\"refcount\": 2, \"references\": [...]}}",
					"outputDataExample": "null"
				}
			],
			"description": "<ul><li>- The core of static analysis is the Disassembly view, which translates machine code into human-readable assembly instructions using the Zydis library</li><li>- Users can navigate the code by following jumps and calls, or by going to any valid address or expression</li><li>- x64dbg can perform control flow analysis (<code>controlflowanalysis</li><li>cpp</code>) to identify functions and basic blocks, which can then be visualized as a graph in the Graph view (<code>DisassemblerGraphView</li><li>cpp</code>)</li><li>- The cross-reference (x-ref) functionality allows users to find all locations in the code that refer to a specific address</li></ul>",
