		"How the command line and scripting works": {
			"name": "How the command line and scripting works",
			"simSteps": [
				{
					"simStepId": "96833474-7463-42fd-baee-075aab0dafe4",
					"diagramNodeId": "abd9e4b3-ddfe-490f-9f1d-7660d5ceeed7",
					"simStepLabel": "Command Flow: User Input",
					"simStepDescription": "The user types a command like `inc rax` or `scriptexec \"C:\\myscript.txt\"` into the GUI's command bar. The GUI sends this command string to a message queue for the debugger's command processing thread.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/dbg/x64dbg.cpp",
						"startLine": "511",
						"endLine": "526",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"gMsgQueue",
							"MsgWait",
							"cmd",
							"newcmd"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"command\": \"inc rax\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"message\": {\"param1\": \"inc rax\"}}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "874b1a88-f1cd-4ef7-8d8b-1f7215ad1b91",
					"diagramNodeId": "084f1f9e-103a-4cb5-98bb-bdf36985c1fa",
					"simStepLabel": "Command Flow: Command String Transmission",
					"simStepDescription": "The `cbCommandProvider` function, acting as the interface between the GUI and the command engine, provides the raw command string to the main command loop.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/dbg/command.cpp",
						"startLine": "288",
						"endLine": "288",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"cbCommandProvider",
							"command_"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"command_string\": \"inc rax; run\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"command_string\": \"inc rax; run\"}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "3f3015b4-c26c-49de-b83d-ac4cf4b1f3af",
					"diagramNodeId": "076c7e7b-c67b-48cd-892d-e2d33910b184",
					"simStepLabel": "Command Flow: Command Splitting",
					"simStepDescription": "The `cmdloop` function receives the command string and calls `cmdsplit` to break it into individual commands based on the semicolon (`;`) separator. This allows for chaining multiple commands.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/dbg/command.cpp",
						"startLine": "281",
						"endLine": "290",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"cmdloop",
							"cmdsplit",
							"command_",
							"commands"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"command_string\": \"inc rax; run\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"commands\": [\"inc rax\", \"run\"]}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "fbacbc4e-c18a-4784-a36c-ff2ef61e5a46",
					"diagramNodeId": "e3b497bb-57e0-4608-b1c7-77ac133223a0",
					"simStepLabel": "Command Flow: Process Individual Command",
					"simStepDescription": "The first command from the split list is passed into the processing loop for execution.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/dbg/command.cpp",
						"startLine": "291",
						"endLine": "291",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"command"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"command\": \"inc rax\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"command\": \"inc rax\"}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "43850d6a-42fe-4c32-9997-24678bbe14b2",
					"diagramNodeId": "11577fa5-40c5-4693-a9d7-f531ef7570d0",
					"simStepLabel": "Command Flow: Command Lookup and Callback",
					"simStepDescription": "Inside the `cmdloop`, `cmdget` finds the registered `COMMAND` structure for the command name (e.g., 'inc'). `cmdexeccallback` is then invoked, which parses arguments and calls the command's specific C++ callback function, in this case `cbInstrInc`.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/dbg/command.cpp",
						"startLine": "297",
						"endLine": "315",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"cmdget",
							"cmdexeccallback",
							"found->cbCommand"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"command\": \"inc rax\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"callback_function\": \"cbInstrInc\", \"args\": [\"inc rax\", \"rax\"]}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "07c91f3c-0142-4339-a657-cebe8747c338",
					"diagramNodeId": "5e08483f-2a7b-48c1-bab1-e4bcb3207e77",
					"simStepLabel": "Command Flow: Command Transformation to Expression",
					"simStepDescription": "Many general-purpose commands are implemented as wrappers around the more powerful expression parser. The `cbInstrInc` callback transforms the command `inc rax` into an equivalent expression string `rax++`.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/dbg/commands/cmd-general-purpose.cpp",
						"startLine": "39",
						"endLine": "44",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"cbInstrInc",
							"cmddirectexec",
							"StringUtils::sprintf"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"argc\": 2, \"argv\": [\"inc rax\", \"rax\"]}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"expression_string\": \"rax++\"}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "0c1d9a7c-58e1-4e6b-b18f-858cb52d5a67",
					"diagramNodeId": "cf6ccd20-517c-4557-984e-4431003622fe",
					"simStepLabel": "Command Flow: Direct Execution / Expression Fallback",
					"simStepDescription": "`cmddirectexec` is called to execute the transformed command `rax++`. It first tries to find a registered command with this name. When it fails, it falls back to treating the string as an expression to be evaluated by the `ExpressionParser`.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/dbg/command.cpp",
						"startLine": "326",
						"endLine": "345",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"cmddirectexec",
							"cmdget",
							"found",
							"ExpressionParser"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"command\": \"rax++\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"is_expression\": true}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "9dda4fa8-2699-4321-8afc-6a2ee01ae283",
					"diagramNodeId": "d39aa878-124a-4df1-8c23-ea7b5215c1c2",
					"simStepLabel": "Command Flow: Expression to Parser",
					"simStepDescription": "The string `rax++` is instantiated as an `ExpressionParser` object and its `Calculate` method is invoked for evaluation.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/dbg/command.cpp",
						"startLine": "343",
						"endLine": "345",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"parser",
							"parser.Calculate"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"expression\": \"rax++\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"expression\": \"rax++\"}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "a02b0feb-2c4c-4841-97cd-50985bc8711c",
					"diagramNodeId": "43801730-e66e-489a-bd22-6ea1d763a137",
					"simStepLabel": "Command Flow: Expression Evaluation",
					"simStepDescription": "The `ExpressionParser::Calculate` method parses the expression. It identifies `rax` as a register, reads its current value, performs the post-increment operation, and writes the new value back to the `rax` register, completing the command.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/dbg/expressionparser.cpp",
						"startLine": "300",
						"endLine": "301",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"ExpressionParser"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"expression\": \"rax++\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"success\": true}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "31f0fba5-8901-4231-9ec4-da4cc520d606",
					"diagramNodeId": "910570e9-40e2-4ae3-9967-6f2150b76205",
					"simStepLabel": "Scripting Flow: User issues 'scriptexec' command",
					"simStepDescription": "The user enters the `scriptexec` command. After being processed by `cmdloop`, the command's registered callback `cbScriptExec` is called.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/dbg/commands/cmd-script.cpp",
						"startLine": "55",
						"endLine": "60",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"cbScriptExec",
							"ScriptExecAwait"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"argc\": 2, \"argv\": [\"scriptexec\", \"C:\\\\myscript.txt\"]}",
					"outputDataExample": "null"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "2280b955-a303-4ffc-a01d-ecdb76ca964a",
					"diagramNodeId": "c1a30a0c-3dc3-422c-bd06-328f9608d3a3",
					"simStepLabel": "Scripting Flow: Filename to Script Engine",
					"simStepDescription": "The script filename is passed from the command callback to the `ScriptExecAwait` function, which manages the script's lifecycle.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/dbg/commands/cmd-script.cpp",
						"startLine": "59",
						"endLine": "59",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"ScriptExecAwait",
							"argv[1]"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"filename\": \"C:\\\\myscript.txt\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"filename\": \"C:\\\\myscript.txt\"}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "82be4420-8561-4b5a-a265-0fcf9b7b960a",
					"diagramNodeId": "2c8b849a-ee2f-4860-86bf-2b11901c3c7d",
					"simStepLabel": "Scripting Flow: Load and Run Script",
					"simStepDescription": "`ScriptExecAwait` queues a task that first calls `scriptLoad` to read and parse the script file into an internal line map. It then calls `scriptRun` to begin executing the script from the first line.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/dbg/simplescript.cpp",
						"startLine": "833",
						"endLine": "843",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"scriptQueue.await",
							"scriptLoad",
							"scriptRun"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"filename\": \"C:\\\\myscript.txt\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "null"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "2ba5bf21-73cf-417a-bbd7-8e69c40830db",
					"diagramNodeId": "c414afb3-2c24-4448-bcf6-6632109cff21",
					"simStepLabel": "Scripting Flow: Script Line to Command Executor",
					"simStepDescription": "Inside the `scriptRun` loop, a command line from the script file (e.g., 'inc rax') is fetched and passed to `cmddirectexec` for execution, bridging the script and command engines.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/dbg/simplescript.cpp",
						"startLine": "520",
						"endLine": "520",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"cmddirectexec",
							"cmd"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"command_line\": \"inc rax\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"command_line\": \"inc rax\"}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "d6cefb4e-8466-45bd-8314-2c450f758227",
					"diagramNodeId": "94454940-4060-4f7e-a84c-aea4d3d21bb9",
					"simStepLabel": "Scripting Flow: Merged Command Execution",
					"simStepDescription": "The script engine has invoked `cmddirectexec`. The execution flow now merges with the standard command flow. `cmddirectexec` will resolve `inc rax` to its callback (`cbInstrInc`), which transforms it to `rax++`, which is finally executed by the `ExpressionParser`.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/dbg/command.cpp",
						"startLine": "326",
						"endLine": "345",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"cmddirectexec"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"command_line\": \"inc rax\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"success\": true}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "6360a6aa-dda5-4460-8e49-27a12bf52c80",
					"diagramNodeId": "d7d0cb27-47d2-43d0-ae11-6357e64062a4",
					"simStepLabel": "Scripting Flow: Result Returns to Script Engine",
					"simStepDescription": "After the command from the script line is executed, `cmddirectexec` returns a success/failure status back to the script engine's `scriptInternalCmdExec` function.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/dbg/simplescript.cpp",
						"startLine": "520",
						"endLine": "528",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"res"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"success\": true}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"success\": true}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "1081c258-b893-4c3a-b57d-5fcac8faed30",
					"diagramNodeId": "0c1996ea-84d1-4973-b85e-fe1aaea2781b",
					"simStepLabel": "Scripting Flow: Script Loop Continues",
					"simStepDescription": "The `scriptInternalCmdExec` function returns a `STATUS_CONTINUE` code, signaling to the `scriptRun` loop that execution was successful and it should proceed to the next line of the script.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/dbg/simplescript.cpp",
						"startLine": "608",
						"endLine": "612",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"bContinue",
							"scriptInternalCmd"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"status\": \"STATUS_CONTINUE\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "null"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "de32e849-e6c7-44a9-80fa-a027bf75f63b",
					"diagramNodeId": "56ece9b8-e4d0-4bfe-aec1-12aa2dd96aef",
					"simStepLabel": "Scripting Flow: Script Completion",
					"simStepDescription": "After the last line of the script is executed, the `scriptRun` function's main loop terminates and the function returns, indicating that the script has finished running.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/dbg/simplescript.cpp",
						"startLine": "839",
						"endLine": "839",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"scriptRun"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "null",
					"outputDataExample": "null"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "b453f349-0bae-4870-b282-776bc20deb96",
					"diagramNodeId": "db48773a-d8ad-42ea-9350-c9c2700e7fb7",
					"simStepLabel": "Scripting Flow: Script Unload",
					"simStepDescription": "Finally, after `scriptRun` completes successfully, `ScriptExecAwait` calls `ScriptUnloadAwait` to clear the loaded script data from memory. The `scriptexec` command is now fully complete.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/dbg/simplescript.cpp",
						"startLine": "841",
						"endLine": "841",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"ScriptUnloadAwait"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "null",
					"outputDataExample": "null"
				}
			],
			"description": "<ul><li>- A command bar at the bottom of the main window allows users to execute powerful text-based commands for automation and control</li><li>- The command system, implemented in <code>command</li><li>cpp</code> and <code>src/dbg/commands/</code>, maps text commands to C++ callback functions</li><li>- Users can chain commands with semicolons or write them into script files (<code></li><li>txt</code>) for execution</li><li>- The expression parser (<code>expressionparser</li><li>cpp</code>) evaluates complex C-style expressions containing registers, symbols, and memory pointers</li></ul>",
			"simulationNodesAndEdges": {
				"abd9e4b3-ddfe-490f-9f1d-7660d5ceeed7": {
