		"How execution tracing works": {
			"name": "How execution tracing works",
			"simSteps": [
				{
					"simStepId": "1b490872-5117-45bb-8bc8-dfd6470cb299",
					"diagramNodeId": "1d6872cc-f613-4495-9676-6175e9191fb0",
					"simStepLabel": "User Starts Trace Recording",
					"simStepDescription": "A user initiates execution tracing by issuing the `StartRunTrace` command, often through the GUI's context menu or by typing it directly. This command is an alias for `StartTraceRecording` and is registered at startup to map to the `cbDebugStartTraceRecording` callback function.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/dbg/x64dbg.cpp",
						"startLine": "271",
						"endLine": "271",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"dbgcmdnew",
							"cbDebugStartTraceRecording",
							"StartRunTrace"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\n  \"command\": \"StartRunTrace \\\"C:\\\\temp\\\\mytrace.log\\\"\"\n}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\n  \"callbackFunction\": \"cbDebugStartTraceRecording\",\n  \"arguments\": [\n    \"C:\\\\temp\\\\mytrace.log\"\n  ]\n}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "aad74351-da5d-47cd-99fd-9dee559131ff",
					"diagramNodeId": "aef62d45-d710-47df-b7e5-ed00511b512b",
					"simStepLabel": "Dispatch Start Trace Command",
					"simStepDescription": "The debugger's command processor parses the user's input and dispatches the command and its arguments to the registered callback function, `cbDebugStartTraceRecording`.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/dbg/commands/cmd-tracing.cpp",
						"startLine": "234",
						"endLine": "239",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"cbDebugStartTraceRecording"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\n  \"command\": \"StartRunTrace\",\n  \"arguments\": [\n    \"C:\\\\temp\\\\mytrace.log\"\n  ]\n}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\n  \"command\": \"StartRunTrace\",\n  \"arguments\": [\n    \"C:\\\\temp\\\\mytrace.log\"\n  ]\n}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "f73b0031-4cdf-428f-82a9-345d3e43ebb4",
					"diagramNodeId": "2782195b-68d7-41dc-9fa4-247e256cab9d",
					"simStepLabel": "Handle Start Trace Command",
					"simStepDescription": "The `cbDebugStartTraceRecording` function is executed. It validates that a filename argument is provided and then calls the `enableTraceRecording` method on the global `TraceRecord` object to begin the recording process.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/dbg/commands/cmd-tracing.cpp",
						"startLine": "234",
						"endLine": "239",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"cbDebugStartTraceRecording",
							"TraceRecord.enableTraceRecording"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\n  \"argc\": 2,\n  \"argv\": [\n    \"StartRunTrace\",\n    \"C:\\\\temp\\\\mytrace.log\"\n  ]\n}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\n  \"call\": \"TraceRecord.enableTraceRecording\",\n  \"arguments\": {\n    \"enabled\": true,\n    \"fileName\": \"C:\\\\temp\\\\mytrace.log\"\n  }\n}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "3d80bc83-e9d5-4300-af1c-b51c7d59d53a",
					"diagramNodeId": "fd567a9c-fff9-4e6c-8b27-754b3f6a178b",
					"simStepLabel": "Request to Enable Recording",
					"simStepDescription": "The command handler invokes the `enableTraceRecording` method, passing `true` to enable tracing and the specified file path.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/dbg/commands/cmd-tracing.cpp",
						"startLine": "238",
						"endLine": "238",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"TraceRecord.enableTraceRecording"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\n  \"enabled\": true,\n  \"fileName\": \"C:\\\\temp\\\\mytrace.log\"\n}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\n  \"enabled\": true,\n  \"fileName\": \"C:\\\\temp\\\\mytrace.log\"\n}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "2d31b772-07ec-4df8-b286-2e1efe190535",
					"diagramNodeId": "21f5a358-3632-41ef-a9c7-1ed812403fe0",
					"simStepLabel": "Initialize Trace File and State",
					"simStepDescription": "The `TraceRecordManager::enableTraceRecording` method sets up the trace file and activates tracing mode. It creates the trace file, writes a JSON header with metadata (like architecture and debuggee hash), sets the internal `rtEnabled` flag to true, and immediately records the state of the current instruction to start the trace log.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/dbg/TraceRecord.cpp",
						"startLine": "486",
						"endLine": "561",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"enableTraceRecording",
							"rtEnabled",
							"rtFile",
							"CreateFileW",
							"WriteFile",
							"TraceExecuteRecord"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\n  \"enabled\": true,\n  \"fileName\": \"C:\\\\temp\\\\mytrace.log\"\n}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\n  \"rtEnabled\": true,\n  \"rtFile\": \"HANDLE:0x12345678\",\n  \"status\": \"Trace recording started.\"\n}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "f6d01205-6cd1-4933-a768-2693bbfbd840",
					"diagramNodeId": "a30f9c10-d181-4c4d-bfb8-6768f0f2170b",
					"simStepLabel": "Debugger Step Occurs",
					"simStepDescription": "With tracing active, the user performs a step in the debugger (e.g., 'Step Into'). The debuggee executes one instruction, then pauses, triggering a debug event.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/dbg/debugger.cpp",
						"startLine": "1303",
						"endLine": "1303",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"cbStep"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\n  \"debuggerAction\": \"StepInto\"\n}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\n  \"debuggerAction\": \"StepInto\"\n}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "a9b704f8-7e7c-4783-8ffa-f21f49eee210",
					"diagramNodeId": "2d5e1d90-6fd7-4bfe-99b4-6a170fdc19d9",
					"simStepLabel": "Execute Step Callback",
					"simStepDescription": "When the debugger pauses after the step, the `cbStep` callback function is executed. This function is the central handler for a single-step event. It updates the GUI state and calls `dbgtraceexecute` to record the instruction that was just executed.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/dbg/debugger.cpp",
						"startLine": "1303",
						"endLine": "1329",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"cbStep",
							"dbgtraceexecute",
							"CIP"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\n  \"debugEvent\": \"SINGLE_STEP\"\n}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\n  \"nextAction\": \"call dbgtraceexecute(CIP)\"\n}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "93b7a537-987c-4fc5-8556-b9cfca94f748",
					"diagramNodeId": "f76aa60e-0d25-4723-99cc-0991cd6298df",
					"simStepLabel": "Invoke Trace Recorder",
					"simStepDescription": "The `cbStep` callback invokes `dbgtraceexecute` with the current instruction pointer (CIP) to log the executed instruction.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/dbg/debugger.cpp",
						"startLine": "1326",
						"endLine": "1326",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"dbgtraceexecute"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\n  \"CIP\": \"0x00401050\"\n}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\n  \"CIP\": \"0x00401050\"\n}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "84aab721-9b66-4311-9938-4a99389d0880",
					"diagramNodeId": "90f5a346-2b51-4e8a-bbd2-66f8b093698d",
					"simStepLabel": "Process and Record Trace Data",
					"simStepDescription": "The `dbgtraceexecute` function orchestrates the recording. It checks if trace recording is enabled. If so, it reads the instruction from memory, disassembles it, and calls `TraceExecuteRecord` to perform the detailed logging of the execution state.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/dbg/TraceRecord.cpp",
						"startLine": "706",
						"endLine": "740",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"dbgtraceexecute",
							"isTraceRecordingEnabled",
							"MemRead",
							"instruction.DisassembleSafe",
							"TraceExecuteRecord"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\n  \"CIP\": \"0x00401050\"\n}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\n  \"instruction\": {\n    \"address\": \"0x00401050\",\n    \"mnemonic\": \"push\",\n    \"operands\": \"ebp\"\n  }\n}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "f37bf0b6-90ad-45e2-a54b-b6997686db81",
					"diagramNodeId": "a8a21488-071c-43f0-b405-842756396e8e",
					"simStepLabel": "Pass Context to File Writer",
					"simStepDescription": "`TraceExecuteRecord` is called with the disassembled instruction object, containing all necessary details to log.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/dbg/TraceRecord.cpp",
						"startLine": "718",
						"endLine": "718",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"TraceExecuteRecord"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\n  \"instruction\": {\n    \"address\": \"0x00401050\",\n    \"bytes\": \"55\",\n    \"mnemonic\": \"push\",\n    \"operands\": \"ebp\"\n  }\n}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\n  \"instruction\": {\n    \"address\": \"0x00401050\",\n    \"bytes\": \"55\",\n    \"mnemonic\": \"push\",\n    \"operands\": \"ebp\"\n  }\n}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "85d78f8c-b21a-4622-9a4d-52137554b9c7",
					"diagramNodeId": "fe8a96b9-8d95-4a8f-b531-b040d671732f",
					"simStepLabel": "Write Delta-Compressed State to File",
					"simStepDescription": "`TraceExecuteRecord` captures the full CPU context (registers, flags), compares it with the previous state to find changes (delta compression), serializes this information into a compact binary format, and writes the resulting buffer to the trace file.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/dbg/TraceRecord.cpp",
						"startLine": "251",
						"endLine": "430",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"TraceExecuteRecord",
							"DbgGetRegDumpEx",
							"rtOldContext",
							"WriteFile",
							"rtFile"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\n  \"newContext\": {\n    \"registers\": {\n      \"EIP\": \"0x00401051\",\n      \"ESP\": \"0x0019FF70\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"oldContext\": {\n    \"registers\": {\n      \"EIP\": \"0x00401050\",\n      \"ESP\": \"0x0019FF74\"\n    }\n  }\n}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\n  \"bytesWritten\": 32\n}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "86ecd74c-91a6-4ea2-a4be-b37bb8149ff2",
					"diagramNodeId": "2ea18998-dd7a-4d24-b634-380d5fe70d83",
					"simStepLabel": "User Issues `StopRunTrace` Command",
					"simStepDescription": "The process of stepping and recording repeats until the user decides to stop the trace by issuing the `StopRunTrace` command.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/dbg/x64dbg.cpp",
						"startLine": "272",
						"endLine": "272",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"dbgcmdnew",
							"cbDebugStopTraceRecording",
							"StopRunTrace"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\n  \"userInput\": \"StopRunTrace\"\n}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\n  \"userInput\": \"StopRunTrace\"\n}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "a32d3e67-9733-489e-b7d2-fc1136cf19b8",
					"diagramNodeId": "56098996-2f19-4ea9-be9d-1dd9eb18626c",
					"simStepLabel": "Handle Stop Trace Command",
					"simStepDescription": "The `cbDebugStopTraceRecording` function is called in response to the user's command. It simply calls the `TraceRecordManager` to disable the recording.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/dbg/commands/cmd-tracing.cpp",
						"startLine": "241",
						"endLine": "244",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"cbDebugStopTraceRecording",
							"TraceRecord.enableTraceRecording"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\n  \"argc\": 1,\n  \"argv\": [\n    \"StopRunTrace\"\n  ]\n}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\n  \"call\": \"TraceRecord.enableTraceRecording\",\n  \"arguments\": {\n    \"enabled\": false,\n    \"fileName\": null\n  }\n}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "fa5c9c1c-2028-4585-a727-fee8e7af49f5",
					"diagramNodeId": "677515a1-1bbc-429d-b3ca-af3ea306d2db",
					"simStepLabel": "Request to Disable Recording",
					"simStepDescription": "The command handler invokes the `enableTraceRecording` method, passing `false` to disable tracing.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/dbg/commands/cmd-tracing.cpp",
						"startLine": "243",
						"endLine": "243",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"TraceRecord.enableTraceRecording"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\n  \"enabled\": false,\n  \"fileName\": null\n}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\n  \"enabled\": false,\n  \"fileName\": null\n}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "01a2323d-c09c-4845-b4b0-3d4d10cff928",
					"diagramNodeId": "27f7e07b-3e40-4651-ba53-2463bb952d1f",
					"simStepLabel": "Finalize Trace File",
					"simStepDescription": "When `TraceRecordManager::enableTraceRecording` is called with `enabled=false`, it closes the handle to the trace file, sets the `rtEnabled` flag to false, and logs a message indicating that trace recording has stopped. This concludes the tracing session.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/dbg/TraceRecord.cpp",
						"startLine": "569",
						"endLine": "580",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"enableTraceRecording",
							"rtEnabled",
							"CloseHandle",
							"rtFile"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\n  \"enabled\": false,\n  \"fileName\": null\n}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\n  \"rtEnabled\": false,\n  \"status\": \"Trace recording stopped.\"\n}"
				}
			],
			"description": "<ul><li>- Execution tracing allows users to record the sequence of executed instructions to understand program flow without manual stepping</li><li>- x64dbg supports 'Run Trace', which records every instruction between two breakpoints, and 'Step Trace', which records each step</li><li>- Conditional tracing can be configured to log messages, execute commands, or break when a specific condition is met during the trace</li><li>- The Trace view provides an interface to browse, search, and analyze the recorded execution history</li></ul>",
			"simulationNodesAndEdges": {
