		"How symbol and source-level debugging works": {
			"name": "How symbol and source-level debugging works",
			"simSteps": [
				{
					"simStepId": "a15b7d41-b3a7-4922-bee3-43fff4c9778b",
					"diagramNodeId": "3075b748-ea7e-40d9-8e07-2c30df52f5e5",
					"simStepLabel": "User Initiates Symbol Download",
					"simStepDescription": "The user right-clicks a module in the Symbol View UI and selects 'Download Symbols for This Module' or 'Download Symbols for All Modules'. This action triggers the corresponding slot to execute a debugger command.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/gui/Src/Gui/SymbolView.cpp",
						"startLine": "717",
						"endLine": "727",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"moduleDownloadSymbols()",
							"moduleDownloadAllSymbols()",
							"DbgCmdExec"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"userAction\": \"Right-click -> Download Symbols for This Module\", \"selectedModule\": \"kernel32.dll\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"command\": \"symdownload \\\"kernel32.dll\\\"\"}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "d7d244e3-24cd-4dfe-a212-2ef0ccc06029",
					"diagramNodeId": "11671eb4-cbdc-4f33-a4ef-d9134c34db99",
					"simStepLabel": "Send 'symdownload' Command",
					"simStepDescription": "The `DbgCmdExec` function sends the 'symdownload' command string from the GUI component to the debugger backend for processing.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/gui/Src/Gui/SymbolView.cpp",
						"startLine": "721",
						"endLine": "721",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"DbgCmdExec"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"command\": \"symdownload \\\"kernel32.dll\\\"\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"command\": \"symdownload \\\"kernel32.dll\\\"\"}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "1a8c2641-f10d-4d28-8979-bb507e3bc52f",
					"diagramNodeId": "8e1fac20-eb34-4f36-a58e-1caddb899802",
					"simStepLabel": "Process 'symdownload' Command",
					"simStepDescription": "The debugger core receives the command, and the registered handler `cbDebugDownloadSymbol` is executed. It determines which module(s) to download symbols for based on the provided arguments.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/dbg/commands/cmd-analysis.cpp",
						"startLine": "182",
						"endLine": "204",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"cbDebugDownloadSymbol",
							"SymDownloadAllSymbols",
							"SymDownloadSymbol"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"command\": \"symdownload\", \"arguments\": [\"kernel32.dll\"]}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"moduleBase\": \"0x7ff8f7b10000\", \"symbolStore\": \"https://msdl.microsoft.com/download/symbols\"}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "748a289d-99f5-4bf7-abc5-aaba4b625d3b",
					"diagramNodeId": "1d11a160-91d0-4b0d-b83f-db05259d9263",
					"simStepLabel": "Invoke Symbol Download Logic",
					"simStepDescription": "`cbDebugDownloadSymbol` calls `SymDownloadSymbol` with the module's base address and the symbol store URL to begin the download process.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/dbg/commands/cmd-analysis.cpp",
						"startLine": "200",
						"endLine": "200",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"SymDownloadSymbol"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"moduleBase\": \"0x7ff8f7b10000\", \"symbolStore\": \"https://msdl.microsoft.com/download/symbols\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"moduleBase\": \"0x7ff8f7b10000\", \"symbolStore\": \"https://msdl.microsoft.com/download/symbols\"}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "657ccbcc-6a7c-42ad-a219-fce898eee9c5",
					"diagramNodeId": "8b0ff6f8-d56f-4cfa-980d-56fe4dcf2c8c",
					"simStepLabel": "Download PDB and Initiate Load",
					"simStepDescription": "`SymDownloadSymbol` constructs the download URL, downloads the PDB file using the `downslib` library, and if successful, calls `MODINFO::loadSymbols` to process the downloaded PDB file.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/dbg/symbolinfo.cpp",
						"startLine": "198",
						"endLine": "354",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"SymDownloadSymbol",
							"downslib_download",
							"info->loadSymbols"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"moduleBase\": \"0x7ff8f7b10000\", \"symbolStore\": \"https://msdl.microsoft.com/download/symbols\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"pdbPath\": \"C:\\\\symbols\\\\kernel32.pdb\\\\12345...\\\\kernel32.pdb\"}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "5c5cd70f-b69b-4551-b7a8-f7d7ae321b73",
					"diagramNodeId": "a37ed889-c857-4a07-856e-99f625051835",
					"simStepLabel": "Pass PDB Path to Module Loader",
					"simStepDescription": "The path to the downloaded PDB file is passed from the symbol handler to the `MODINFO::loadSymbols` method for the specific module.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/dbg/symbolinfo.cpp",
						"startLine": "348",
						"endLine": "348",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"info->loadSymbols",
							"szSymbolPath"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"pdbPath\": \"C:\\\\symbols\\\\kernel32.pdb\\\\12345...\\\\kernel32.pdb\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"pdbPath\": \"C:\\\\symbols\\\\kernel32.pdb\\\\12345...\\\\kernel32.pdb\"}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "96effe84-c9f7-4d18-8f6b-cfe5078c735d",
					"diagramNodeId": "a227f5bc-b31a-4569-974f-fbdc65eb2429",
					"simStepLabel": "Create DIA Source and Load PDB",
					"simStepDescription": "`MODINFO::loadSymbols` instantiates a `SymbolSourceDIA` object, which is responsible for handling PDB files using the Debug Interface Access (DIA) SDK. It then calls the `loadPDB` method to begin parsing.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/dbg/module.cpp",
						"startLine": "1402",
						"endLine": "1425",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"MODINFO::loadSymbols",
							"SymbolSourceDIA",
							"symSource->loadPDB"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"pdbPath\": \"C:\\\\symbols\\\\kernel32.pdb\\\\12345...\\\\kernel32.pdb\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"pdbPath\": \"C:\\\\...\\\\kernel32.pdb\", \"modname\": \"kernel32.dll\", \"imageBase\": \"0x7ff8f7b10000\", \"imageSize\": \"0x100000\"}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "d8b8ad1f-54a5-4e51-bb1c-f38a6116cf41",
					"diagramNodeId": "dccb5749-33d0-40aa-a80f-a2b410129830",
					"simStepLabel": "Pass PDB Info to SymbolSourceDIA",
					"simStepDescription": "Module information such as its name, base address, size, and PDB validation data (GUID, age, signature) is passed to `SymbolSourceDIA::loadPDB`.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/dbg/module.cpp",
						"startLine": "1421",
						"endLine": "1421",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"symSource->loadPDB"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"pdbPath\": \"C:\\\\...\\\\kernel32.pdb\", \"modname\": \"kernel32.dll\", \"imageBase\": \"0x7ff8f7b10000\", \"imageSize\": \"0x100000\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"pdbPath\": \"C:\\\\...\\\\kernel32.pdb\", \"modname\": \"kernel32.dll\", \"imageBase\": \"0x7ff8f7b10000\", \"imageSize\": \"0x100000\"}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "c08a3c69-0cb8-4a7d-8177-565d7359d4bd",
					"diagramNodeId": "ae655592-a257-40e9-abdc-89a6516a6eb5",
					"simStepLabel": "Validate PDB and Start Async Threads",
					"simStepDescription": "`SymbolSourceDIA::loadPDB` uses a `PDBDiaFile` object to open the PDB and validate its signature against the module's debug information. If valid, it creates and starts two background threads: one for symbols (`loadSymbolsAsync`) and one for source lines (`loadSourceLinesAsync`).",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/dbg/symbolsourcedia.cpp",
						"startLine": "45",
						"endLine": "70",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"SymbolSourceDIA::loadPDB",
							"PDBDiaFile",
							"pdb.open",
							"CreateThread",
							"SymbolsThread",
							"SourceLinesThread"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"pdbPath\": \"C:\\\\...\\\\kernel32.pdb\", \"modname\": \"kernel32.dll\", \"validationData\": {\"guid\": \"...\", \"age\": 1}}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"status\": \"Validation successful, async loading started\"}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "8e081735-a54d-42ab-a6b3-1f706e24aca4",
					"diagramNodeId": "7127ac1a-09e0-4b24-9922-c510a977c38c",
					"simStepLabel": "Request PDB Symbol Enumeration",
					"simStepDescription": "The background symbol-loading thread (`loadSymbolsAsync`) invokes `PDBDiaFile::enumerateLexicalHierarchy` to begin recursively reading all symbol data from the PDB file.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/dbg/symbolsourcedia.cpp",
						"startLine": "165",
						"endLine": "165",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"pdb.enumerateLexicalHierarchy"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{}",
					"outputDataExample": "{}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "fae0bf1a-b24a-4b18-98f0-862dc1cc1803",
					"diagramNodeId": "ede633c5-30b4-4117-b09f-c63ef9c89843",
					"simStepLabel": "Enumerate Symbols with DIA SDK",
					"simStepDescription": "`PDBDiaFile::enumerateLexicalHierarchy` uses the DIA SDK interfaces (`IDiaSession`, `IDiaSymbol`, `IDiaEnumSymbols`) to find and iterate through all symbols (publics, functions, data, etc.) within the PDB file.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/dbg/pdbdiafile.cpp",
						"startLine": "570",
						"endLine": "673",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"PDBDiaFile::enumerateLexicalHierarchy",
							"m_session->get_globalScope",
							"globalScope->findChildren",
							"enumSymbols->Next"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"symbol\": {\"name\": \"CreateFileW\", \"rva\": \"0x2a050\", \"type\": \"Function\"}}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "9d67f095-5d65-4c2e-87c6-88c94fd89876",
					"diagramNodeId": "15c1e0e9-e9a5-4882-9b76-0c2980917a6c",
					"simStepLabel": "Stream Symbols via Callback",
					"simStepDescription": "As `PDBDiaFile` finds each symbol, it invokes the callback function provided by `SymbolSourceDIA`, passing the raw symbol data back to the caller for processing.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/dbg/symbolsourcedia.cpp",
						"startLine": "131",
						"endLine": "163",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"query.callback"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"symbol\": {\"name\": \"CreateFileW\", \"rva\": \"0x2a050\", \"type\": \"Function\"}}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"symbol\": {\"name\": \"CreateFileW\", \"rva\": \"0x2a050\", \"type\": \"Function\"}}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "8de1ecf9-eeba-49fc-8617-9e451ebfff27",
					"diagramNodeId": "f2deb9df-dc31-40dd-80ea-14512e43aca8",
					"simStepLabel": "Cache and Index Symbols",
					"simStepDescription": "`SymbolSourceDIA` receives the raw symbol data, converts it to its internal `SymbolInfo` format, and stores it in a vector (`_symData`). After enumeration, it creates sorted maps for fast lookups by both address and name.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/dbg/symbolsourcedia.cpp",
						"startLine": "173",
						"endLine": "237",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"_symData",
							"_symAddrMap",
							"_symNameMap",
							"std::sort"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"symbolStream\": [{\"name\": \"...\"}]}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"status\": \"Symbols cached and indexed\"}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "9047ee4c-32f6-4973-9a5f-0b25898bc135",
					"diagramNodeId": "0507469c-386d-4f1d-8ecc-ca82a95d740e",
					"simStepLabel": "Notify GUI of Symbol Update",
					"simStepDescription": "After symbol loading and processing are complete, `SymbolSourceDIA` calls `GuiInvalidateSymbolSource`. This sends a message to the GUI, indicating that the symbol data for the module has changed and the UI should be refreshed.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/dbg/symbolsourcedia.cpp",
						"startLine": "249",
						"endLine": "249",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"GuiInvalidateSymbolSource"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"imageBase\": \"0x7ff8f7b10000\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"imageBase\": \"0x7ff8f7b10000\"}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "c987c75d-348c-4519-86e5-3d09054cd583",
					"diagramNodeId": "6ddf81a6-a48a-4adf-b982-a6257239bbe0",
					"simStepLabel": "User Selects Module in Symbol View",
					"simStepDescription": "In the GUI, the user clicks on a module in the module list within the `SymbolView`. This triggers the `moduleSelectionChanged` slot, initiating the process to display symbols for that module.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/gui/Src/Gui/SymbolView.cpp",
						"startLine": "442",
						"endLine": "480",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"moduleSelectionChanged",
							"mModuleList"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"userAction\": \"Click on module 'ntdll.dll'\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"selectedModuleBase\": \"0x7ff8f9e10000\"}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "8135a2a0-a769-463e-95e5-7891c227d88c",
					"diagramNodeId": "6c01860d-7a5c-49e1-863a-4122cea7d8a7",
					"simStepLabel": "Request Symbol Enumeration via Bridge",
					"simStepDescription": "The `moduleSelectionChanged` slot calls the bridge function `DbgSymbolEnum` to request the list of all symbols associated with the selected module's base address.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/gui/Src/Gui/SymbolView.cpp",
						"startLine": "459",
						"endLine": "463",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"DbgSymbolEnum"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"base\": \"0x7ff8f9e10000\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"base\": \"0x7ff8f9e10000\"}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "622bde13-f0dd-4a8d-8cf1-38adc7b33367",
					"diagramNodeId": "f9936a44-14ca-4a4f-8a98-fb49d7800425",
					"simStepLabel": "Bridge Transmits Symbol Enum Request",
					"simStepDescription": "The `DbgSymbolEnum` function in the bridge layer sends a `DBG_SYMBOL_ENUM` message to the debugger core, packaging the module base address and the callback information.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/bridge/bridgemain.cpp",
						"startLine": "1105",
						"endLine": "1116",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"DbgSymbolEnum",
							"_dbg_sendmessage",
							"DBG_SYMBOL_ENUM"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"base\": \"0x7ff8f9e10000\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"message\": \"DBG_SYMBOL_ENUM\", \"payload\": {\"base\": \"0x7ff8f9e10000\"}}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "07f22cea-5a5d-4ee3-8ded-313955521839",
					"diagramNodeId": "8fe149a8-6c8a-4ff7-91dc-1f80819f6ba7",
					"simStepLabel": "Retrieve Symbols from Cache",
					"simStepDescription": "The debugger core's message handler calls `SymEnum`. This function retrieves the module's information and accesses the already-loaded symbols from the `SymbolSourceDIA` object associated with that module.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/dbg/symbolinfo.cpp",
						"startLine": "1",
						"endLine": "1",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"SymEnum",
							"ModInfoFromAddr",
							"modInfo->symbols->enumSymbols"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"base\": \"0x7ff8f9e10000\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"symbolCachePointer\": \"...\"}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "9be7b897-45b8-4aa1-8af5-4f15b40a1bcd",
					"diagramNodeId": "f81abddd-1220-4b25-84be-33036406a873",
					"simStepLabel": "Return Symbol Data via Callback",
					"simStepDescription": "The `enumSymbols` method in `SymbolSourceDIA` iterates through its cached `SymbolInfo` vector. For each symbol, it invokes the provided callback, passing a `SYMBOLPTR` that points to the cached data, which propagates back to the GUI.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/dbg/symbolsourcedia.cpp",
						"startLine": "473",
						"endLine": "508",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"enumSymbols",
							"cbEnum",
							"_symData"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"symbolCachePointer\": \"...\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"symbolPtr\": {\"modbase\": \"0x7ff8f9e10000\", \"symbol\": \"...\"}}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "64f737f2-d53c-454e-8722-42caf5672aa0",
					"diagramNodeId": "622214bb-e5c0-482c-a1a7-d32e9b8825de",
					"simStepLabel": "Collect Symbol Data in GUI",
					"simStepDescription": "The callback function, implemented as a lambda in `SymbolView`, is executed for each symbol. It collects the `SYMBOLPTR`s into a local vector.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/gui/Src/Gui/SymbolView.cpp",
						"startLine": "459",
						"endLine": "463",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"info",
							"userdata",
							"data"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"symbolPtr\": {\"modbase\": \"0x7ff8f9e10000\", \"symbol\": \"...\"}}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"symbolPtr\": {\"modbase\": \"0x7ff8f9e10000\", \"symbol\": \"...\"}}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "b49173d6-85af-44e9-ad16-e48975457961",
					"diagramNodeId": "1db697c4-5d7a-4810-b376-f845bc10e715",
					"simStepLabel": "Populate Symbol List UI",
					"simStepDescription": "Once the enumeration is complete, the `SymbolView` takes the collected vector of symbol pointers, moves it into the `ZehSymbolTable` data model, and updates the UI table to display the new list of symbols for the selected module.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/gui/Src/Gui/SymbolView.cpp",
						"startLine": "466",
						"endLine": "477",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"mSymbolSearchList",
							"mList->mData",
							"mList->setRowCount",
							"mList->reloadData"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"symbols\": [{\"modbase\": \"...\", \"symbol\": \"...\"}, ...]}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"status\": \"UI updated with symbol list\"}"
				}
			],
			"description": "<ul><li>- x64dbg can download and load symbol files (PDB) to resolve addresses to meaningful function and variable names</li><li>- The Symbol view (<code>SymbolView</li><li>cpp</code>) lists all loaded modules and allows browsing of their exported and public symbols</li><li>- When symbols with source information are loaded, the Source view (<code>SourceView</li><li>cpp</code>) can display the original source code, linking it to the corresponding assembly instructions</li><li>- The DIA (Debug Interface Access) SDK is used to parse PDB files, as seen in <code>symbolsourcedia</li><li>cpp</code></li></ul>",
			"simulationNodesAndEdges": {
