		"How exception handling works": {
			"name": "How exception handling works",
			"simSteps": [
				{
					"simStepId": "2206f3af-d029-451b-ae5d-c773df0b9d27",
					"diagramNodeId": "",
					"simStepLabel": "OS Delivers Debug Event",
					"simStepDescription": "The operating system sends an EXCEPTION_DEBUG_INFO structure to the debugger via the debug event loop.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/dbg/debugger.cpp",
						"startLine": "2936",
						"endLine": "2936",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"SetCustomHandler",
							"UE_CH_UNHANDLEDEXCEPTION",
							"cbException"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\n  \"dwDebugEventCode\": 1,\n  \"dwProcessId\": 1234,\n  \"dwThreadId\": 5678,\n  \"u\": {\n    \"Exception\": {\n      \"ExceptionRecord\": {\n        \"ExceptionCode\": \"0xC0000005\",\n        \"ExceptionFlags\": 0,\n        \"ExceptionAddress\": \"0x00401050\",\n        \"NumberParameters\": 2,\n        \"ExceptionInformation\": [1, 0]\n      },\n      \"dwFirstChance\": 1\n    }\n  }\n}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\n  \"dwDebugEventCode\": 1,\n  \"dwProcessId\": 1234,\n  \"dwThreadId\": 5678,\n  \"u\": {\n    \"Exception\": {\n      \"ExceptionRecord\": {\n        \"ExceptionCode\": \"0xC0000005\",\n        \"ExceptionFlags\": 0,\n        \"ExceptionAddress\": \"0x00401050\",\n        \"NumberParameters\": 2,\n        \"ExceptionInformation\": [1, 0]\n      },\n      \"dwFirstChance\": 1\n    }\n  }\n}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "398890fe-1ab6-471e-8896-62e5403fab54",
					"diagramNodeId": "4c29a848-07d1-42a8-9087-11a17b0f83b1",
					"simStepLabel": "Exception Handler Entry Point",
					"simStepDescription": "The debug loop receives the debug event and calls `cbException`, the main handler for all exceptions. It updates the last exception info and notifies the GUI.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/dbg/debugger.cpp",
						"startLine": "2093",
						"endLine": "2101",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"cbException",
							"ExceptionData",
							"ExceptionCode",
							"GuiSetLastException",
							"lastExceptionInfo"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\n  \"ExceptionData\": {\n    \"ExceptionRecord\": {\n      \"ExceptionCode\": \"0xC0000005\",\n      \"ExceptionAddress\": \"0x00401050\"\n    },\n    \"dwFirstChance\": 1\n  }\n}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\n  \"lastExceptionInfo\": {\n    \"ExceptionRecord\": {\n      \"ExceptionCode\": \"0xC0000005\",\n      \"ExceptionAddress\": \"0x00401050\"\n    },\n    \"dwFirstChance\": 1\n  },\n  \"lastExceptionCode\": \"0xC0000005\"\n}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "68bfbc35-794b-4648-8b84-712477af202f",
					"diagramNodeId": "e6750efd-78cd-4bed-ab03-e92ea59ea528",
					"simStepLabel": "Check for Custom Exception Breakpoint",
					"simStepDescription": "The handler first checks if a specific breakpoint for this exception code has been set by the user via the `SetExceptionBPX` command.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/dbg/debugger.cpp",
						"startLine": "2105",
						"endLine": "2105",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"BpGet",
							"BPEXCEPTION"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\n  \"ExceptionCode\": \"0xC0000005\",\n  \"BreakpointType\": \"BPEXCEPTION\"\n}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\n  \"ExceptionCode\": \"0xC0000005\",\n  \"BreakpointType\": \"BPEXCEPTION\"\n}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "ec9e0cb8-797e-4531-9671-b7523877da7f",
					"diagramNodeId": "bca6f3a2-05bd-470d-84aa-9485f96ece5a",
					"simStepLabel": "Custom Breakpoint Path vs. Filter Path",
					"simStepDescription": "The execution path diverges here. If a custom exception breakpoint (`SetExceptionBPX`) exists for the exception code, `cbGenericBreakpoint` is called to handle it like a normal breakpoint. If not, the debugger proceeds to check the general exception filters defined in the settings.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/dbg/debugger.cpp",
						"startLine": "2104",
						"endLine": "2114",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"BpGet",
							"cbGenericBreakpoint",
							"dbggetexceptionfilter"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\n  \"ExceptionCode\": \"0xC0000005\"\n}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\n  \"path_taken\": \"Filter Path (No custom BP found)\"\n}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "a1e6d8e7-73c0-4c0a-801f-aff64614c52a",
					"diagramNodeId": "0d999fa6-4415-4694-9a78-e045f9d72b36",
					"simStepLabel": "Retrieve General Exception Filter",
					"simStepDescription": "Since no specific exception breakpoint was found, the system requests the general filter settings that apply to this exception code.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/dbg/debugger.cpp",
						"startLine": "2114",
						"endLine": "2114",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"dbggetexceptionfilter"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\n  \"ExceptionCode\": \"0xC0000005\"\n}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\n  \"ExceptionCode\": \"0xC0000005\"\n}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "fcc30b21-c611-402f-836d-bf73d8dab948",
					"diagramNodeId": "ed7560a7-b1bd-459c-ab2b-647898749e82",
					"simStepLabel": "Apply Exception Filter Rules",
					"simStepDescription": "The `dbggetexceptionfilter` function returns the appropriate filter. The `cbException` function then uses this filter to decide whether to break, whether to log, and how to continue (pass the exception to the debuggee or swallow it).",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/dbg/debugger.cpp",
						"startLine": "2145",
						"endLine": "2171",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"ExceptionData",
							"filter",
							"logException",
							"breakOn",
							"dwFirstChance",
							"dbgsetcontinuestatus",
							"bSkipExceptions"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\n  \"filter\": {\n    \"range\": {\"start\": \"0xC0000005\", \"end\": \"0xC0000005\"},\n    \"breakOn\": \"FirstChance\",\n    \"logException\": true,\n    \"handledBy\": \"Debuggee\"\n  },\n  \"ExceptionData\": {\n    \"dwFirstChance\": 1\n  }\n}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\n  \"decision\": {\n    \"should_break\": true,\n    \"log_exception\": true,\n    \"continue_status\": \"DBG_EXCEPTION_NOT_HANDLED\"\n  }\n}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "5011b00a-342e-4690-87c8-034bcd53e623",
					"diagramNodeId": "daf2b160-7cab-40ec-a7ea-3645f1131178",
					"simStepLabel": "Set Continue Status",
					"simStepDescription": "Based on the filter's 'Handled By' setting, the debugger sets the continue status for the upcoming `ContinueDebugEvent` call. `DBG_EXCEPTION_NOT_HANDLED` passes the exception to the application's handlers, while `DBG_CONTINUE` swallows it.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/dbg/debugger.cpp",
						"startLine": "3105",
						"endLine": "3109",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"dbgsetcontinuestatus",
							"nextContinueStatus",
							"SetNextDbgContinueStatus"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\n  \"status\": \"DBG_EXCEPTION_NOT_HANDLED\"\n}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\n  \"status\": \"DBG_EXCEPTION_NOT_HANDLED\"\n}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "08ead610-8fe9-43db-8417-9fa04fd5669c",
					"diagramNodeId": "7446b2c4-b36e-4ee3-9b58-59c2db9aa360",
					"simStepLabel": "Pause Debugger and Wait for User",
					"simStepDescription": "If the filter settings determine that the debugger should break, the GUI is updated to a 'paused' state, the debug loop is locked, and the system waits for user interaction. Plugin callbacks for pausing and exceptions are fired.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/dbg/debugger.cpp",
						"startLine": "2173",
						"endLine": "2185",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"DebugUpdateGuiSetStateAsync",
							"lock",
							"bPausedOnException",
							"plugincbcall",
							"CB_PAUSEDEBUG",
							"CB_EXCEPTION",
							"wait"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\n  \"break_decision\": true\n}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\n  \"debugger_state\": \"paused\"\n}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "94f60b7c-ad2b-461b-845c-982a7e3d05b7",
					"diagramNodeId": "c9f14853-7f1b-4221-9509-ae345ea11a2d",
					"simStepLabel": "User Issues 'erun' Command",
					"simStepDescription": "After the debugger pauses, the user decides to continue execution but wants to ignore any subsequent first-chance exceptions. They issue the `erun` (exception-run) command.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "",
						"startLine": "0",
						"endLine": "0",
						"relevantVariables": []
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\n  \"command\": \"erun\"\n}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\n  \"command\": \"erun\"\n}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "8fb57243-eff8-4afa-b455-99595000769d",
					"diagramNodeId": "b6e16ad5-ecfa-49de-849f-71de65f8c872",
					"simStepLabel": "Enable 'Skip Exceptions' Flag",
					"simStepDescription": "The `erun` command handler `cbDebugErun` calls `dbgsetskipexceptions(true)`. This sets an internal flag that will cause the `cbException` function to immediately return for any subsequent first-chance exceptions, effectively ignoring them.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/dbg/commands/cmd-debug-control.cpp",
						"startLine": "356",
						"endLine": "357",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"cbDebugErun",
							"dbgsetskipexceptions"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\n  \"skip\": true\n}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\n  \"bSkipExceptions\": true\n}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "713a387a-2917-4421-a8ac-65e519a5dbca",
					"diagramNodeId": "ea62e5c9-76d9-4cbc-8248-30a31e312133",
					"simStepLabel": "User Issues 'con' Command",
					"simStepDescription": "Alternatively, the user can change how the *current* exception is handled by using the 'con' (continue) command. With no arguments, it swallows the exception. With an argument, it passes it to the debuggee.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "",
						"startLine": "0",
						"endLine": "0",
						"relevantVariables": []
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\n  \"command\": \"con\"\n}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\n  \"command\": \"con\"\n}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "60d60766-161f-4c8c-9a69-e0e9c6ac84f0",
					"diagramNodeId": "6947b6d2-96c6-4b5b-93aa-e5d359423274",
					"simStepLabel": "Update Continue Status for Current Exception",
					"simStepDescription": "The `cbDebugContinue` handler is executed. It calls `dbgsetcontinuestatus` again, overwriting the value set by the exception filter with the user's explicit choice (either `DBG_CONTINUE` or `DBG_EXCEPTION_NOT_HANDLED`). This alters the behavior when the debugger is eventually resumed.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/dbg/commands/cmd-debug-control.cpp",
						"startLine": "433",
						"endLine": "446",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"cbDebugContinue",
							"dbgsetcontinuestatus",
							"DBG_CONTINUE",
							"DBG_EXCEPTION_NOT_HANDLED"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\n  \"argc\": 1,\n  \"argv\": [\"con\"]\n}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\n  \"nextContinueStatus\": \"DBG_CONTINUE\"\n}"
				}
			],
			"description": "<ul><li>- The debugger intercepts exceptions that occur in the debuggee, such as access violations or breakpoints</li><li>- Users can configure the debugger to ignore certain exceptions, break on the first chance, or break on the second (unhandled) chance</li><li>- Custom exception breakpoints (<code>SetExceptionBPX</code>) can be set for specific exception codes to trigger debugger breaks</li><li>- The debugger can then pass the exception back to the application or <code>swallow</code> it to alter the program's flow</li></ul>",
			"simulationNodesAndEdges": {
				"4c29a848-07d1-42a8-9087-11a17b0f83b1": {
					"simStepIds": [
						"398890fe-1ab6-471e-8896-62e5403fab54"
