			],
			"description": "<ul><li>- The functionality of x64dbg can be extended via a C-based plugin API</li><li>- Plugins are DLLs that export specific functions like <code>pluginit</code> and <code>plugsetup</code> which are called by the debugger on load</li><li>- The plugin SDK (<code>_plugins</li><li>h</code>, <code>_plugin_types</li><li>h</code>) allows plugins to register new commands, add items to GUI menus, and subscribe to debugger events (callbacks) like process creation or hitting a breakpoint</li><li>- The <code>plugin_loader</li><li>cpp</code> handles the discovery, loading, and initialization of plugins from the <code>plugins</code> directory</li></ul>",
